{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off","id":1558364,"title":"Query from a Casual - Why is the Garou Nation so much worse off?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-02-17T13:01:02-08:00","id":1558364,"title":"Query from a Casual - Why is the Garou Nation so much worse off?","content":"One complaint I'm seeing a lot of is that 5th Edition is much harder on the Garou and nothing but how much they suck.<br /> <br /> However, I remember 1st Edition Werewolf and early 2nd Edition. In fact, that's &quot;my&quot; W:TA because I didn't follow up on Revised and other works.<br /> <br /> The point was that the Garou had failed and the Apocalypse was imminent...because of all the reasons given in the 5th Edition book about them being too violent, unable to get over their differences tribally, and the Children of Gaia being ignored. It was why Evan-White-Boy-Saves-Us ( :kidding, kidding: ) existed as his whole thing. The Garou needed to make serious systemic change or everyone was screwed.<br /> <br /> I'm not a big fan of 5E's take but I am curious why this specific complaint is coming up because it seems like it was just following up from the original presentation that all of the War of Rage, Impergium, and other things had come to roost.<br /> <br /> Change or die and all that.<br /> <br /> I wonder if this is related to the editions I missed and the fact that 5E was going back to the original versions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 02-17-2026, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-20T00:58:53-08:00","id":1558390,"title":"","content":"Because its leadership, direction and organization completly collapsed and the only tribe with anything resembling an idea of how to go forward went nuts.<br /> <br /> Oh and albrecht is just his dad now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-20T02:08:44-08:00","id":1558391,"title":"","content":"W5 is a reboot<br /> Or more like WW5 is a re-imagining not a continuation<br /> <br /> It shares some names but not the history and context of the setting<br /> The history of the WW5 Garou is vague and unclear and neither they nor the spirits can resolve this<br /> There is no Kinfolk<br /> There is no Crinos born Garou<br /> There is no Gnosis<br /> All powers use Rage or Willpower to activate them<br /> Crinos requires you to kill things, spend willpower or frenzy so it lost a lot of utility<br /> It's much easier to lose the wolf now when you spend Rage, and you're stuck without shapeshifting/gifts until you are able to howl at the moon<br /> The tribes still exist, but they are now more akin to Totem mystery cults than cultures<br /> The Garou can only enter the Umbra through rituals and if the spend too long there they start getting damage<br /> <br /> Essentially W5 is to W20 and previous editions what Forsaken is to them. You'll see a lot of familiar stuff, but essentially it's had such massive and fundamental changes as to be a different game entirely. (Like V5 to be honest)<br /> <br /> If you look it from a different angle?<br /> Gaia is dead or dying, most of the old Garou Heroes are gone, the Umbra has changed and the Garou Nation is no more.<br /> What is left is a bunch of werewolf kids who have no clue what the world was look like when Gaia was still kicking. This means they are mostly lost and have to figure out stuff on their own but have also the chance, not to repeat the mistakes of their predecessors.<br /> Not quite make a sense, but... would fly<br /> But if you really really like to make sense of the changes beyond \u201cthe company decided to change things\u201d, they left surprisingly many space to fill the gaps even though the official statement is \u201cthis is a new thing, don\u2019t think about the old one\u201d.<br /> <br /> <br /> Why WW5 - or the WW5 Garou Nation is so much worse than previous editions?<br /> <br /> One of the key struggles of the Garou now are two mental states; fanatical rage and hopelessness.<br /> But more importantly?<br /> They lost basically everything that made them a Gartou - they are Werewolves... but not Garou<br /> They lost their identiy, lore, spirituality, spirit world, Crinos form, and basically any- and everything that made them Garou and Garou Nation<br /> <br /> The previous editions were not flawless, not at all, they had their problem, but 1st Edition Werewolf and early 2nd Edition had a <i>setting</i> . They had a world crafted behind them with full of mysteries that made <i>sense</i> even if it was a bit hard to follow and swallow.<br /> The Nation had difficulties, and the existance of Tribes basically was a sign itself the Garou drifted away from the original idea Gaia had: to be the Garou, be her Claws and Deffenders - instead they started to follow spirits who gave them power in turn for their &quot;loyalty and devotion&quot; (I'm pretty sure the Garou original , racial totem been what is now The <i>Old Wolf of the Woods</i> who many still see as their spiritual father...) and with that came different views and interpretations of their Duty and even if not forgot totally they are all Garou, the Human side and the Totem's goals shaped the Tribes so much they were for example Shadowlords first then Garou second<br /> It was not necesarily a bad thing per see, since it was a logical decline rooted in several things and those things snowballed<br /> But still they had an <i>identity </i><br /> <br /> In WW5?<br /> It is not the continuation of the previous editions, the decades old and refined metaplot and setting nor the continuation or the result of a process and progressing (or regressing...) from point A to point B to point C untill you reach the WW5 setting<br /> WW5 is not the result of the Wars of Rage and Tears and Shame , nor the Impergium, nor the Garou fragmentation in to Tribes or the Apocalypse, it was not because the Garou made bad choices and now have to live and die wit hthe consequences; they not &quot;forgot&quot; their own history or connection to the Spirit World and Spirits because all of those things burried the Nation like an avalanche and destroyed it<br /> <br /> It is hard to compare the two setting when they are basically two different games - just WW5 tries to self itself and tries to build on as the &quot;heir&quot; of those previous editions while demolished and ignored it altogteher to build itself up like a frankensteinian mostrosity that would put a Tzimsice Vhozd to shame<br /> <br /> The problem is, it is not followed up what you described<br /> It lost everything 1st Edition Werewolf, 2nd Edition, Revised or WW20 had and what made those werwolves a Garou and their setting<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 02-20-2026, 08:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-20T06:05:44-08:00","id":1558394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is hard to compare the two setting when they are basically two different games - just WW5 tries to self itself and tries to build on as the &quot;heir&quot; of those previous editions while demolished and ignored it altogteher to build itself up like a frankensteinian mostrosity that would put a Tzimsice Vhozd to shame</div> </div> </div> </div>I think part of the problem may be that it's sells itself as a diferent game, but but it's actually this frankensteinian thing.<br /> <br /> The impression I'm given it's that W5 does depend on his previous game for the lore and mood: There's no notion of what was lost if you don't remember the Garou Nation. And there's no failure to be angry against or hopeless about other than that past. There's a vague idea that things could be been different than what's in the Old Lore, but no real tool to make it so beyond that vague memory loss. And the books keep digging on past events and characters whenever they want to create new W5 lore. Or am I wrong?<br /> <br /> H5, for all I loathed it because it felt lke a scam and erased from existance a gameline I liked ... it realy is it's own thing. You don't need to know anything about Hunter: The Reckoning to play it (it's probably better if you don't). V5 it's more relevant to it than HtR. It has it's own &quot;spirit&quot; so to speak, as a game about people angry against the system and monsters. I'm not given that impression from W5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-20T07:57:03-08:00","id":1558395,"title":"","content":"I think the biggest thing that gives W5 the vibe of being too hard on Garou in my opinion is the decision to nuke the Garou Nation. On one hand, it takes the air out of a lot of points of tension in the setting. Because what is even the point of bemoaning the flaws of the Litany? The Garou Nation is gone. Or conflicts between Septs, Tribes or Packs. It's less about striving to overcome and deal with the flaws and more just making the flaws the natural status quo. And on the other hand, despite this fallen and failed nature of the setting, it's just rehashing quite a lot of things from previous editions. It's assumed you play Gaia-loyal Garou in a Pack that might belong to a Sept where still the same old Moots happen and most of the time the goal is to fight the Wyrm. That's what makes it feel so much like this Frankenstein thing, I think. <br /> <br /> The Garou Nation is gone and a failure but the game has done next to nothing to explore the notion of &quot;So now what?&quot;. It just goes back a lot to old stuff strangely.<br /> <br /> And as an aside, I think another issue is that with the new stuff W5 is doing, between W5, previous editions and WtF the W5 ideas are comparatively the least interesting ones. Like Kinfolk from previous editions, Wolfblooded from Forsaken and the Kin in W5. The last one is the blandest one of those. Or take Tribes. Even with the more lore-light approach of Forsaken, those Tribes are more interesting than what W5 has done with Tribes. Especially how Moonlit Path explored Tribal Patron Spirits. Now in W5, Tribes just revolve around the Patron Spirits looking for Garou with certain character traits and getting the Spirits favor comes with various demands and expectations. But that's pretty much it. I understand the idea of getting away from tying the Tribes to human ethnicity and culture but in the end it really has turned into more of a &quot;throwing the baby out with the bathwater&quot; situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-20T09:43:56-08:00","id":1558396,"title":"","content":"Why don't I save anyone reading the thread some time and go metatextual? Because the people that PDX got to run their RPG afterthought hate W:tA and wanted to make it full of angst. There's a reason that the Mage fans are all dreading the shadow of M5 on the horizon, and that's because it was even less like V:tM in its approach to tormenting players (and sometimes their characters too).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558390#post1558390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because its leadership, direction and organization completly collapsed and the only tribe with anything resembling an idea of how to go forward went nuts.<br /> <br /> Oh and albrecht is just his dad now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Grandfather, actually. His parents were implied to have died young in the Legacy Rite comic, or at least younger than his Garou grandfather, based on what he tells Evan after Evan realizes out loud that he wasn't tripping and BSDs really did kill his mother and father. Albrecht himself should have just been left dead with the other major players in the Apocalypse, but PDX is positively Giovanni/Heketa-esque in its want to dig up corpses and do unspeakable things to them. And that's why we have a patchwork of Apocalypse and Forsaken made with ill-fitting pieces of both, like somewhere between a Promethean and a Stolen Moon (and given the text of some super edgy necromancy rituals of old, probably with some... additions best left unmentioned).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-20T15:51:45-08:00","id":1558399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off#post1558364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One complaint I'm seeing a lot of is that 5th Edition is much harder on the Garou and nothing but how much they suck.<br /> <br /> However, I remember 1st Edition Werewolf and early 2nd Edition. In fact, that's &quot;my&quot; W:TA because I didn't follow up on Revised and other works.<br /> <br /> The point was that the Garou had failed and the Apocalypse was imminent...because of all the reasons given in the 5th Edition book about them being too violent, unable to get over their differences tribally, and the Children of Gaia being ignored. It was why Evan-White-Boy-Saves-Us ( :kidding, kidding: ) existed as his whole thing. The Garou needed to make serious systemic change or everyone was screwed.<br /> <br /> I'm not a big fan of 5E's take but I am curious why this specific complaint is coming up because it seems like it was just following up from the original presentation that all of the War of Rage, Impergium, and other things had come to roost.<br /> <br /> Change or die and all that.<br /> <br /> I wonder if this is related to the editions I missed and the fact that 5E was going back to the original versions.</div> </div> </div> </div>As you said, they couldn't get over their tribal differences. The Garou Nation wasn't perfect, but at the very least it provided a means for the disparate tribes to come to the negotiation table and work out some means of cooperation.<br /> <br /> But NOW, there is no Garou Nation, because it's collapsed. Meaning that Garou Society has effectively devolved into a free for all, with everybody running around like a bunch of chickens with their heads cut off.<br /> <br /> <br /> --------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> Let's take a look at the state of the tribes in pre-W5<br /> <br /> Gorgon, the original patron of the Black Furies before they switched to Pegasus, wants to genocide the entirety of the male gender from the face of the earth.<br /> <br /> The Uktena and the Windego both blame the white man for every hardship that has befallen them, and want to genocide us from the face of the earth.<br /> <br /> The Red Talons absolutely despise humanity as a species, and want to genocide every man, woman, child and homid kinfolk from the face of the earth.<br /> <br /> Yeah, that's at least 4 tribes who believe that life will get better for them, if they slaughter millions / billions of people.<br /> <br /> The Garou Nation was keeping them on a leash, and now that leash has snapped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-20T16:13:53-08:00","id":1558400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558399#post1558399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Let's take a look at the state of the tribes in pre-W5<br /> <br /> Gorgon, the original patron of the Black Furies before they switched to Pegasus, wants to genocide the entirety of the male gender from the face of the earth.<br /> <br /> The Uktena and the Windego both blame the white man for every hardship that has befallen them, and want to genocide us from the face of the earth.<br /> <br /> The Red Talons absolutely despise humanity as a species, and want to genocide every man, woman, child and homid kinfolk from the face of the earth.<br /> <br /> Yeah, that's at least 4 tribes who believe that life will get better for them, if they slaughter millions / billions of people.<br /> <br /> The Garou Nation was keeping them on a leash, and now that leash has snapped.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue is that W5 ignores all of that.<br /> <br /> Because as far as W5 is concerned that never happened. Black Furies are a Tribe about vengeance and a sense of justice <i>in general</i>. The focus on feminism is gone. The Older Brother and Younger Brother Tribe have new names with Ghost Council and Galestalkers. Those new versions have no opinions on any human culture or ethnicity. Red Talons are a Tribe that wants to reduce &quot;human dominance &quot; but it's a Tribe with a lot of wolfborn Garou and no concern over who qualifies to join the Tribe. So human-born Red Talons aren't abnormal in W5. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-20T18:37:43-08:00","id":1558402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558399#post1558399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As you said, they couldn't get over their tribal differences. The Garou Nation wasn't perfect, but at the very least it provided a means for the disparate tribes to come to the negotiation table and work out some means of cooperation.<br /> <br /> But NOW, there is no Garou Nation, because it's collapsed. Meaning that Garou Society has effectively devolved into a free for all, with everybody running around like a bunch of chickens with their heads cut off.</div> </div> </div> </div>They seemed to be able to get over those differences in Revised in some variety of functional manner. Then, though, the end of Revised is Apocalypse, and after that? It's over. Go home. Oh, you're expecting a teaser for Werewolf 2? Too bad, it's not even close to finished and the new WoD won't have anything to do with this one. You'll play these scenarios for a while, put the book away until you're 30, and get a little sadder every time you see it on the shelf.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let's take a look at the state of the tribes in pre-W5 </div> </div> </div>?<br /> <br /> Pre-W5 is a very ambiguous term. But you seem to be insinuating that it was in W20 or Revised the last time we saw them, so...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gorgon, the original patron of the Black Furies before they switched to Pegasus, wants to genocide the entirety of the male gender from the face of the earth. </div> </div> </div>No, the Gorgons had split into five different Incarnae, two of whom didn't want to do that, one of whom really wanted to (Medusa), and two who would just kick someone in the dick if they presumed to have control over her but still wouldn't be on track for it. Pegasus, meanwhile, was still quite firmly the tribal patron. There was also a Metamorphic Plague to deal with, but I'm not sure if that plot thread managed to get developed before WW blew the setting up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Uktena and the Windego both blame the white man for every hardship that has befallen them, and want to genocide us from the face of the earth. </div> </div> </div>Older Brother definitely didn't, as they'd opted to expand around the world to network oppressed indigenous people instead and leverage them to make a difference. Younger Brother is still divided and hateful, though I can say &quot;Understandable&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Red Talons absolutely despise humanity as a species, and want to genocide every man, woman, child and homid kinfolk from the face of the earth. </div> </div> </div>Also understandable. They are wolves, wolves got reduced down to near nothing by human actions, and the Talons see no friends in humanity because humanity has given them few to no reasons to think otherwise. However, the Warders of the Land are the majority of the tribe, and they tend to just want humanity away from them, which is easy to do, because no Red Talon caern is close to a major human population center unless the humans try to expand further out, which the Warders view them as having no need to do, with humans having already ruined everywhere else and all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, that's at least 4 tribes who believe that life will get better for them, if they slaughter millions / billions of people. </div> </div> </div>Just one, and the Red Talons are objectively correct about that. Life would get better for wolves, and therefore them, without humans in the picture overflowing every possible habitat and populations in Europe losing their shit about being around wolves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Garou Nation was keeping them on a leash, and now that leash has snapped. </div> </div> </div>No, actually, they just happened to be low in number, largely, out in the middle of nowhere, and up against enemies even in rural locales, making them politically very weak. You think the Wyrm sleeps on the wilderness? Not a chance. That's what keeps most of the Red Talons and Younger Brother occupied. Sometimes, the Wyld also is a problem, and the Furies know well of the danger of an Abscess forming in a caern.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, assumptions that W5 makes are at odds with the lore of the setting. If the Garou Nation no longer exists, Renown should also have gone down the tubes. The Garou Nation wasn't just a large body of werewolves, it also formed a spirit pact that set up everything involving Rank recognition, the spirits agreeing to teach Gifts, etc. W5 ignores this and thinks it can just lean into the way Forsaken did things. Gaia dying would mean that the lights all go out, very swiftly, and all life promptly dies. Again, W5 ignores this as the actual state of things, because it just wants to wallow in angst, Vampire-style, and damn the setting integrity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-20T22:25:18-08:00","id":1558403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558402#post1558402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No, the Gorgons had split into five different Incarnae, two of whom didn't want to do that, one of whom really wanted to (Medusa), and two who would just kick someone in the dick if they presumed to have control over her but still wouldn't be on track for it. Pegasus, meanwhile, was still quite firmly the tribal patron. There was also a Metamorphic Plague to deal with, but I'm not sure if that plot thread managed to get developed before WW blew the setting up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Older Brother definitely didn't, as they'd opted to expand around the world to network oppressed indigenous people instead and leverage them to make a difference. Younger Brother is still divided and hateful, though I can say &quot;Understandable&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also understandable. They are wolves, wolves got reduced down to near nothing by human actions, and the Talons see no friends in humanity because humanity has given them few to no reasons to think otherwise. However, the Warders of the Land are the majority of the tribe, and they tend to just want humanity away from them, which is easy to do, because no Red Talon caern is close to a major human population center unless the humans try to expand further out, which the Warders view them as having no need to do, with humans having already ruined everywhere else and all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Just one, and the Red Talons are objectively correct about that. Life would get better for wolves, and therefore them, without humans in the picture overflowing every possible habitat and populations in Europe losing their shit about being around wolves.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hey, if the writers of 5th edition are going to accuse the entire Get of being Nazi's because of one sub-faction that they personally exterminated, then I'm going to hold the other tribes to the same standard. Especially since they didn't follow the Get's example and allowed them to fester.<br /> <br /> I'm still not entirely sold on the idea of Gaia being the progenitor of everything. The Wyld is the spirit of creation itself; so how could Gaia create something before the very concept of creation existed? Likewise, Weaver is the spirit who gives form and purpose to whatever crazy shit emerges out of Wyld's imagination. If anything, it sounds like Wyld and Weaver created Gaia, because without them, there would be no universe.<br /> <br /> Last time Gaia threatened to off herself if the Triat didn't behave, it only got them to settle down for a brief period. Before they eventually called her bluff and went back to fighting.<br /> <br /> Wyld has a back up copy of Pangaea sitting around in his closet somewhere, gathering dust. If Gaia truly is out of the picture, he can just pull it out and go back to square one. Likewise, the Ananasi are trying to replace Weaver with their queen.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, there's evidence throughout the metaplot that this battle with the Wyrm has been going on for eons. A cyclical nature of the universe being destroyed and recreated over and over again. Those 'qlippothic' realms that the Nephandi draw their power from are even speculated to have been the remains of previous universe that were destroyed.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-21T02:35:23-08:00","id":1558404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558403#post1558403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Hey, if the writers of 5th edition are going to accuse the entire Get of being Nazi's because of one sub-faction that they personally exterminated, then I'm going to hold the other tribes to the same standard. Especially since they didn't follow the Get's example and allowed them to fester.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that the Glorious Fist of Wotan still existed apart from the Swords of Heimdall. They were Get that wanted to kill humans on account of being humans; shunned, but not exterminated. Same as the Eire, later Mother's Fundamentalists of the Fianna. A number of tribes had a very fringe group that wanted to do this and had membership that was probably accounted for greater trouble than the Red Talons. Certainly, the Bone Gnawer Maneaters probably numbered more than the Talons' Lodge of the Predator Kings.<br /> <br /> Or, we could just not follow shit examples like the Cult of Fenris. It was a terrible idea, after all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm still not entirely sold on the idea of Gaia being the progenitor of everything. The Wyld is the spirit of creation itself; so how could Gaia create something before the very concept of creation existed? Likewise, Weaver is the spirit who gives form and purpose to whatever crazy shit emerges out of Wyld's imagination. If anything, it sounds like Wyld and Weaver created Gaia, because without them, there would be no universe. </div> </div> </div>Even if we go with the interpretation that Gaia is under the Triat, that doesn't mean that you get to outlast Gaia. It just means that the Triat might eventually decide to create something new, long after everything has gone dark, assuming that they even return to a state where they can cooperate again. No guarantees there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Last time Gaia threatened to off herself if the Triat didn't behave, it only got them to settle down for a brief period. Before they eventually called her bluff and went back to fighting. </div> </div> </div>That's not a thing that happened.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wyld has a back up copy of Pangaea sitting around in his closet somewhere, gathering dust. If Gaia truly is out of the picture, he can just pull it out and go back to square one. Likewise, the Ananasi are trying to replace Weaver with their queen. </div> </div> </div>The Near Realm Pangaea is not exactly doing well at the time of the Apocalypse (check the Last Battleground scenario; the Elder Serpent is sick with magic prion disease), and it can't exactly serve as a backup copy of Gaia if it's technically Gaia's living heart and She is dead. Also, Ananasa is still stuck in the Opal Prison, and the only time it was close to compromised in any way, shape, or form was with the sacrifice of a lot of unified Garou and Fera.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, there's evidence throughout the metaplot that this battle with the Wyrm has been going on for eons. A cyclical nature of the universe being destroyed and recreated over and over again. Those 'qlippothic' realms that the Nephandi draw their power from are even speculated to have been the remains of previous universe that were destroyed. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Evidence&quot; and &quot;speculated&quot; do not belong in the same thought space. Kind of like &quot;Werewolf&quot; and &quot;Mage&quot;. If something is true in Mage, it might not exist in Werewolf. Like all outer space outside the asteroid belt being the Umbra, for example; that only applies to Mage. In Werewolf, the Aetherial Realm is the Penumbra of everything off of Earth, the planet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-21T03:45:08-08:00","id":1558405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558391#post1558391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">SNIP<br /> \u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>You know I wonder how it held up to BNS version of the nation? As far as I know it's intact but split between two separate political blocs (The western and Eastern Conrdats which roughly maps to traditionalists and progressives), dispute the fact that apparently nearly all the Cearns in north America was blown up in a apcolypise.<br /> <br /> Hell the Fan Game based on BNS actually expanded on that by having the more progressive faction actively rebuild the nation by reclaiming the ruined cairns and even looking to assist the local Fera in that endeavor While the more traditional tribes by contrast are a well ... kinda lack direction ever since to that king albrict sacrificed himself to stop the apocalypse from getting worse than &quot;just&quot; blowing up most of the cearns in America so they kinda stick to they own cearns at least from what little preview material I've seen.<br /> <br /> Like one complainant I've have for this project is that the team are kinda biased towards Eastern Conrdats. Most of the Fluff is told from a POV member of a east-con affiliated tribe and the intro comic is mostly have east con characters except a Get arguing with a Red talon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-21T09:14:25-08:00","id":1558412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558404#post1558404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even if we go with the interpretation that Gaia is under the Triat, that doesn't mean that you get to outlast Gaia. It just means that the Triat might eventually decide to create something new, long after everything has gone dark, assuming that they even return to a state where they can cooperate again. No guarantees there.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You kind of do, because we know that reincarnation is a thing that happens in World of Darkness. Not just among the Fera, but also among Mages, Changelings, even some Paths of Enlightenment still believe in it. Argument could be made about Wraiths, too, depending on what you think happens when you finally pass on.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558404#post1558404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That's not a thing that happened.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I am positive that I've heard before Gaia once threatened to destroy herself, because she was so frustrated with the Triat.<br /> <br /> This got them to calm down, until the Wyrm eventually realized it was the spirit of destruction incarnate, and that the universe destroying itself was therefor no threat to it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558404#post1558404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> &quot;Evidence&quot; and &quot;speculated&quot; do not belong in the same thought space. Kind of like &quot;Werewolf&quot; and &quot;Mage&quot;. If something is true in Mage, it might not exist in Werewolf. Like all outer space outside the asteroid belt being the Umbra, for example; that only applies to Mage. In Werewolf, the Aetherial Realm is the Penumbra of everything off of Earth, the planet.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Whether or not it exists is entirely up to the Story Teller, due to the whole 'unreliable narrator' angle they chose to go with. If this were Chronicles, I would totally agree with you on this. But the metaplot for WoD tries to blend all the splats into a single setting. So we have to figure out how that works.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-21T18:00:40-08:00","id":1558424,"title":"","content":"Offering a good faith reading of the W5 metaplot progression, I think it suffers from two diametrically opposing approaches. One wants to serve as a continuation and progression of the setting as it previously existed and one wants to shake things up and go a radical new direction. I don\u2019t have an issue with either option in theory and would be willing to judge the product of either avenue on its own merits but trying to do both at once is necessarily going to lead to, at minimum, a muddled and internally confused product.<br /> <br /> Obviously a continuation of the previously established status quo was the safest option, that\u2019s essentially what W20 was (alongside some experiments with optional metaplot progression and trying to create a final unified set of rules). But after you do that once with W20, why would you need to do that again? A new edition, to justify itself, would necessitate shaking things up either mechanically or narratively (probably both) but would risk alienating a section of fans.<br /> <br /> IMO I don\u2019t have an issue with \u2018Gaia is on its deathbed and the Nation is shattered\u2019 as the conceit for doing a Werewolf story but it would probably be better served by being a \u2018Dark Mirrors\u2019 style alternate setting. This would let the writers off the hook and give them permission to shake things up, slaughter sacred cows, and really present a radically different setting and mode of play. No guarantee that it would take with the majority of readers but it would probably get a fan base of its own at the very least.<br /> <br /> (Like how in comics you can\u2019t really mess around too much with a character\u2019s mainline status quo but you can do whatever you want in an alternate universe book [not gonna make a judgement on if that\u2019s actually good for comic books in the long term as a medium but it\u2019s a thing because, on some level, it really does just work]).<br /> <br /> tl;dr: It\u2019s hard to simultaneously satisfy corporate mandates and the tendency towards franchise conservatism while also telling a radically different and new story, so if you\u2019re in that position you should probably just decide to do one or the other and then succeed or fail on the merits of the product and it\u2019s reception","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-21T18:15:54-08:00","id":1558425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558424#post1558424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Offering a good faith reading of the W5 metaplot progression, I think it suffers from two diametrically opposing approaches. One wants to serve as a continuation and progression of the setting as it previously existed and one wants to shake things up and go a radical new direction. I don\u2019t have an issue with either option in theory and would be willing to judge the product of either avenue on its own merits but trying to do both at once is necessarily going to lead to, at minimum, a muddled and internally confused product.<br /> <br /> Obviously a continuation of the previously established status quo was the safest option, that\u2019s essentially what W20 was (alongside some experiments with optional metaplot progression and trying to create a final unified set of rules). But after you do that once with W20, why would you need to do that again? A new edition, to justify itself, would necessitate shaking things up either mechanically or narratively (probably both) but would risk alienating a section of fans.</div> </div> </div> </div>And how does that comperes to BNS since as Far as I know The Cearns blowing up is mainly serve as a rest button for setting more than anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-21T18:57:48-08:00","id":1558426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558412#post1558412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You kind of do, because we know that reincarnation is a thing that happens in World of Darkness. Not just among the Fera, but also among Mages, Changelings, even some Paths of Enlightenment still believe in it. Argument could be made about Wraiths, too, depending on what you think happens when you finally pass on.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if they all get fed into the metaphorical chipper-shredder of corruption and destruction (possibly with a side of Oblivion), they won't be coming back in whatever follows. That's what we're looking at - passing past the event horizon and swirling around the end. Everything gets crushed and jumbled up, and has no relation to what follows, except perhaps that they might have recycled some raw materials, maybe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am positive that I've heard before Gaia once threatened to destroy herself, because she was so frustrated with the Triat.<br /> <br /> This got them to calm down, until the Wyrm eventually realized it was the spirit of destruction incarnate, and that the universe destroying itself was therefor no threat to it. </div> </div> </div>[CITATION NEEDED]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whether or not it exists is entirely up to the Story Teller, due to the whole 'unreliable narrator' angle they chose to go with. If this were Chronicles, I would totally agree with you on this. But the metaplot for WoD tries to blend all the splats into a single setting. So we have to figure out how that works. </div> </div> </div>Some lines were fonder of unreliable narrators than others. And also, many elements of WoD metaplot tell the other games to go fuck themselves because they have a very strong setup for exploring something that another game ignores completely. In this case, W:tA tells M:tA to get bent about the Umbra; it was Werewolf's stomping ground to begin with, Mage is just a visitor, and no one really wants to hear all of Mage's strongly Hermetic &quot;Um, ackshully&quot; takes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-21T20:30:56-08:00","id":1558429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558426#post1558426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[CITATION NEEDED]</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Most of my more in depth knowledge about the setting come from the <b>Galliard Group</b>. They have a channel on youtube where they regularly cover deep lore dive videos about World of Darkness, as well as do play sessions of the game. They primarily focus on Werewolf content, if that wasn't obvious, but they also cover Vampire, Mage and Changeling, with a bit about Wraith thrown in.<br /> <br /> Just a heads up though, the Galliard Group are passionate fans, not corporate shills. They give their honest, unfiltered takes and opinions about the game, so there is the risk that they might say something you or others find offensive.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558426#post1558426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Some lines were fonder of unreliable narrators than others. And also, many elements of WoD metaplot tell the other games to go fuck themselves because they have a very strong setup for exploring something that another game ignores completely. In this case, W:tA tells M:tA to get bent about the Umbra; it was Werewolf's stomping ground to begin with, Mage is just a visitor, and no one really wants to hear all of Mage's strongly Hermetic &quot;Um, ackshully&quot; takes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Was it theirs first? Because when the Demons emerged from the Abyss, they had no idea what the Fera were, or where they came from. They didn't exist prior to their imprisonment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-21T20:56:11-08:00","id":1558430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558429#post1558429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Most of my more in depth knowledge about the setting come from the <b>Galliard Group</b>. They have a channel on youtube where they regularly cover deep lore dive videos about World of Darkness, as well as do play sessions of the game. They primarily focus on Werewolf content, if that wasn't obvious, but they also cover Vampire, Mage and Changeling, with a bit about Wraith thrown in.<br /> <br /> Just a heads up though, the Galliard Group are passionate fans, not corporate shills. They give their honest, unfiltered takes and opinions about the game, so there is the risk that they might say something you or others find offensive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, if only there were a way to Crack Slam someone on a forum...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Was it theirs first? Because when the Demons emerged from the Abyss, they had no idea what the Fera were, or where they came from. They didn't exist prior to their imprisonment. </div> </div> </div>Werewolf was written before everything but Vampire, and is the first place where the Umbra was written, so yes. Yes it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-21T21:23:56-08:00","id":1558433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558430#post1558430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Werewolf was written before everything but Vampire, and is the first place where the Umbra was written, so yes. Yes it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, the &quot;um actually&quot; take is the entire premise behind the Ascension War.<br /> <br /> Technocracy and Traditionalists all arguing with each other about how reality is supposed to work. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-21T21:28:36-08:00","id":1558434,"title":"","content":"So like, with V5, it's a direct continuation of the previous Vampire games. It's built on the same setting, it uses the same metaplot. There are differences, like the Banu Haqim joining the Camarilla, or the the Ministry/Setite split, but this is all just a matter of the metaplot moving forward. With W5, it's essentially a new game that reuses a lot of the ideas from older editions, but also removes a lot of important foundational concepts. You can't even really call it a retcon, since much of the old continuity doesn't exist. For all intents and purposes, it's a new game with a new setting.<br /> <br /> Previously, the central theme of WtA was hope. Even if the world was dying, it wasn't dead just yet, and every action the Garou took helped to stave off Gaia's death by another day. Yes, corporations were killing Gaia out of greed and humanity out of apathy, but things weren't completely hopeless. In contracts, in W5, it's a game about playing in a hopeless world. Gaia is already dead. It's too late to turn back the clock and save her. The only faction that hasn't completely given up hope and is raging and trying to do something are biggest villains in the setting. At it's core, W5 is about trying to find some meaning in a world without hope. The story is much more personal - its' not about saving the world, it's about trying to save the people close to you.<br /> <br /> But thematically it's also kind of a mess. It's still a punk game, but it's in an odd spot. Prior editions &quot;the Man&quot; was the capitalist, consumerist world. In the new edition &quot;the Man&quot; is sort of the Garou Nation that failed and allowed Gaia to die. But the Garou nation doesn't really exist anymore. So the Man is sort of the tribal elders, but the Tribes aren't as big of a thing either. So you're kind of being a punk against the elder Garou at your local Cairn and it doesn't really carry the same weight. <br /> <br /> In the end there's a lot of mechanical changes from prior editions, there's a lot of setting changes, there's a lot of other changes. All of this combines to make W5 extremely different from prior Werewolf games. It's not quite as extreme as the change between the old Hunter and the new one, but it's still much more significant than the change Vampire got, and a lot of people aren't terribly thrilled about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-21T22:08:00-08:00","id":1558435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558434#post1558434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But thematically it's also kind of a mess. It's still a punk game, but it's in an odd spot. Prior editions &quot;the Man&quot; was the capitalist, consumerist world. In the new edition &quot;the Man&quot; is sort of the Garou Nation that failed and allowed Gaia to die. But the Garou nation doesn't really exist anymore. So the Man is sort of the tribal elders, but the Tribes aren't as big of a thing either. So you're kind of being a punk against the elder Garou at your local Cairn and it doesn't really carry the same weight.</div> </div> </div> </div>So i'ts a game about playing the stereotypical punk coded slacktavist? Who scream about the Injustice of the world but doing little to change them?<br /> <br /> Like I personally think a WtA game should at least take cues from LANCER like sure I sometimes find it come across overtly simplstic and ham handed on how it handle it's themes at times but it's makes it clear that the players can have a genune chance to make things better even if it's only one plant out of countless thousands. <br /> <br /> Also a reliviant quote from Deadlock: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Fe3RBFYNuXA\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Fe3RBFYNuXA</a><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Vindicta:</b> Billy, you scream of the ills of the world, but do nothing to change them.<br /> <br /> <b>Billy:</b> Lady, I wake people up, I speak truth to power. What the hell do you do other than walk around Central Park barefoot?!<br /> <br /> <b>Vindicta:</b> <i>I'm</i> systematically murdering the bloodline of a judge that used his power to sentence innocent women to death. And in the process, I'm dismantling an extremist neopolitical movement. But <i>do</i> tell me about how important your soapbox is.<br /> <br /> <b>Billy:</b> The, uh... The ritual's starting. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-21T23:02:22-08:00","id":1558436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558434#post1558434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The story is much more personal - its' not about saving the world, it's about trying to save the people close to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is fundamentally stupid, because if the world is dead, they're gonna die with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558435#post1558435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So i'ts a game about playing the stereotypical punk coded slacktavist? Who scream about the Injustice of the world but doing little to change them?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much in W5, yes. Game was WAY different before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-21T23:09:04-08:00","id":1558437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558435#post1558435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So i'ts a game about playing the stereotypical punk coded slacktavist? Who scream about the Injustice of the world but doing little to change them?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a bit more complicated than that and a lot of it comes through the metatext.<br /> <br /> The only faction that's out there crusading against the Wyrm are literal Nazis. You, as a player, aren't supposed to want to emulate Nazis. So doing thar same hing the Cult if Fenris is doing is bad.<br /> <br /> This goes back to a central idea in the game, that you can't beat the Wyrm by being a raging ball of violence and rage. The White Howlers fell because they tried to beat the Wyrm with violence. The Cult of Fenris is falling to the Wyrm (if they haven't already) because of their use of extreme violence. Even the Garou Nation fell because they preferred to use violence. <br /> <br /> The player Garou aren't any different either. They're not going to beat the Wyrm and save Gaia (if you even can) through violence. To beat the Wyrm, instead of violence they'll need to...<br /> <br /> And that's the thing. The Garou <i>are</i> balls of violence and rage. There's no escaping that. This is the &quot;buy in&quot; for players in W5. They're playing a monster of rage and violence in a game where rage and violence can't save the world (Gaia is dead and the world is doomed). <br /> <br /> Where prior editions of Werewolf were more about never giving up because there's always a sliver of hope, W5 is more about accepting that even if everything is doomed, you can still find things to fight for and protect. It's a pretty massive change in mood and theme.<br /> <br /> This is also why the game is more &quot;street level.&quot; You're not out there crusading to save the world (that's what the Nazis are doing and it's a lost cause). Instead you're buying your loved ones and community as much time as possible before the inevitable end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-22T00:54:42-08:00","id":1558438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558437#post1558437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is also why the game is more &quot;street level.&quot; You're not out there crusading to save the world (that's what the Nazis are doing and it's a lost cause). Instead you're buying your loved ones and community as much time as possible before the inevitable end.</div> </div> </div> </div>But then the obvious argument aginst that is that save the world and you're own commuinty? Again I circled back to LANCER where saving the as much of the people as possible is objectively the best coarse of action. Like by W5 logic then LANCER it's Nazi propaganda.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 02-22-2026, 04:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-22T03:22:07-08:00","id":1558440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558438#post1558438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But then the obvious argument aginst that is that save the world and you're own commuinty? Again I circled back to LANCER where saving the as much of the people as possible is objectively the best coarse of action. Like by W5 logic then LANCER it's Nazi propaganda.</div> </div> </div> </div>So like, the basic idea in W5 is that you <i>can't</i> save the world. It's too late. Gaia is already dead. The Garou may have had the chance to save her but they failed. The world is just her corpse and she's going to start rotting soon. <br /> <br /> This is the &quot;buy in&quot; for players, that they're willing to play characters in a doomed timeline for which there is no happy end. It's about finding something beautiful and choosing to protect it efor as long as possible, even in the face of inevitable destruction. <br /> <br /> This isn't even m necessarily all that weird. There are tons of stories across cultures about doomed people standing up against impossible odds and choosing to fight to protect their family or home despite knowing that death was the only possible outcome. <br /> <br /> That's the kind if story W5 is intended to tell, about a group of monsters on a dying world whose ancestors failed them and now they're doing their best to keep the people they care about alive as long as possible before the world eventually collapses.<br /> <br /> That is a huge change from previous Werewolf games. It's not a power fantasy in the least and I suspect it's not the kind of game that most players want to play, especially players coming from previous Werewolf editions where the core idea was that it was never too late and s long as you kept fighting they're was always a chance that this could get better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-22T04:44:04-08:00","id":1558441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558440#post1558440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> That is a huge change from previous Werewolf games. It's not a power fantasy in the least and I suspect it's not the kind of game that most players want to play, especially players coming from previous Werewolf editions where the core idea was that it was never too late and s long as you kept fighting they're was always a chance that this could get better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honstly I still feel like this w5 is going about that premise the wrong way since at the end of the day people still fight for a community and W5 bearly provides on that front.<br /> <br /> Like by contrast BNS fan game I'd mentioned already have all the cearns been blown up by the apocalypse but nation still survived if divided and at least half still made an effort to rebuild.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-22T06:29:26-08:00","id":1558444,"title":"","content":"While it isn't directly a part of W5's take on the WtA-setting, I think the mechanics also give an impression of the designers' pessimistic attitude towards the Garou. One of the most relevant elements in this regard are the Harano/Hauglost-tracks. These are two tracks that trigger checks in various story-related situations and if you fail those, you get a dot in either Harano or Hauglosk. Additionally, you can add a point to either for some immediate &quot;healing&quot; (a full WP-regeneration or immediately filling up your Rage-track to 5). But Touchstones only allow you to switch a dot from one track to the other and besides that, the only way to actually reduce the number of dots in those tracks is to get a specific usable Talisman (in other words, it's up to the ST's generosity whether you have access to that or not). And the moment you hit 5 dots in either the Harano- or the Hauglosk-track, your character is immediately rendered unplayable. So, most of the time, every W5-Garou-PC is automatically engaged in this kind of doomspiral. And that isn't just a harsh mechanic compared to previous WtA-editions, it's harsh compared to the other two WOD5E-games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-22T07:03:22-08:00","id":1558447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558438#post1558438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But then the obvious argument aginst that is that save the world and you're own commuinty? Again I circled back to LANCER where saving the as much of the people as possible is objectively the best coarse of action. Like by W5 logic then LANCER it's Nazi propaganda.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only, and I mean ONLY reason why the Get of Fenris were turned into literal Nazi's in W5, is because their tribal culture was based on Nordic / Scandinavian vikings.<br /> <br /> Any claims that they were being used by white supremacists to spread hate speech are complete bullshit. Nazi's have other things to do, than spend hours of their weekly schedule role playing with a bunch of nerdy goths and furries.<br /> <br /> ---------------------<br /> <br /> When the Get of Fenris learned that SOME of their tribe had fallen in with the Nazi regime, they personally took it upon themselves to eradicate them. A feat which they spent literal decades trying to accomplish (somewhere between 30 to 60 years).<br /> <br /> Then along comes 5th edition, which flips the script and says everybody in the Get are white supremacists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-22T09:39:47-08:00","id":1558449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558433#post1558433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, the &quot;um actually&quot; take is the entire premise behind the Ascension War.<br /> <br /> Technocracy and Traditionalists all arguing with each other about how reality is supposed to work. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>And they can go and do that in some other corner of the universe as long as no one else has to be in it. But the ship's sailed there, so, hindsight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only, and I mean ONLY reason why the Get of Fenris were turned into literal Nazi's in W5, is because their tribal culture was based on Nordic / Scandinavian vikings. </div> </div> </div>Not so much since Revised. A lot of names from Norse/Germanic myths still get used, but the later tribebook had them be defined more as the tribe that celebrates and obsesses over hypercompetence and stoicism. Part of that arguably makes them closer to modern US culture, and in particular some bits of the USMC. Kind of a funny reversal, as the Revised tribebook was written by an actual Scandanavian author and the typical accusations that the WoD focuses too much on the USA.<br /> <br /> (And WoD5 focuses on Europe to the exclusion of all else! I guess it's okay when it happens over there [/sarcasm])<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Any claims that they were being used by white supremacists to spread hate speech are complete bullshit. Nazi's have other things to do, than spend hours of their weekly schedule role playing with a bunch of nerdy goths and furries.<br /> <br /> ---------------------<br /> <br /> When the Get of Fenris learned that SOME of their tribe had fallen in with the Nazi regime, they personally took it upon themselves to eradicate them. A feat which they spent literal decades trying to accomplish (somewhere between 30 to 60 years).<br /> <br /> Then along comes 5th edition, which flips the script and says everybody in the Get are white supremacists. </div> </div> </div>Always true, but we have been ruminating over that since James Sembrano's Patreon posts revealed the reason why being completely and utterly metatextual (i.e. the creative director). Now, apparently European LARPs are a bit of a different deal and you might actually see racist Odinists about, as attested by some of the European members of the forums, but the Revised tribebook should have been license to shoot that dead on sight, since someone who reveres Odin would probably have been torn apart by the Get before they got anywhere near a rite of passage. The tribe does regard him as sworn enemy number one behind the direct forces of the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-22T10:17:19-08:00","id":1558452,"title":"","content":"I'm a US based poster, and I can attest to multiple experiences with people trying to use the Swords to smuggle Nazi shit into games (both TTRPG at conventions and LARP). It might not be so widespread as to be a huge problem, but it's not bullshit either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-22T13:08:46-08:00","id":1558456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558447#post1558447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The only, and I mean ONLY reason why the Get of Fenris were turned into literal Nazi's in W5, is because their tribal culture was based on Nordic / Scandinavian vikings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is really weird and I suspect a form if projection from the writers.<br /> <br /> <br /> Well in contrast to that to how they portrayed in the (at time of this post still unrelased) fan game where my impression from reading the preview material they're the only western concordat tribe (besides the glass Walkers though they're technically east con &quot;defectors&quot;) that's bother to take the initiative in trying to recover the nation rather than brood in they cearns.<br /> <br /> To the piont they're the only west con tribe have any presence in the fluff beyond they tribe write up in an otherwise easten concordat dominant book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-22T14:00:04-08:00","id":1558457,"title":"","content":"I feel like Werewolf Fifth Edition made things a lot worse for the Garou Nation than they had been in any of the previous editions, especially the Twentieth Anniversary one, which was relatively optimistic by comparison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-22T14:17:33-08:00","id":1558458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558456#post1558456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is really weird and I suspect a form if projection from the writers.<br /> <br /> <br /> Well in contrast to that to how they portrayed in the (at time of this post still unrelased) fan game where my impression from reading the preview material they're the only western concordat tribe (besides the glass Walkers though they're technically east con &quot;defectors&quot;) that's bother to take the initiative in trying to recover the nation rather than brood in they cearns.<br /> <br /> To the piont they're the only west con tribe have any presence in the fluff beyond they tribe write up in an otherwise easten concordat dominant book.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're sort of right.<br /> <br /> Pre-W5, the tribes were predominantly based around specific cultures or ethnic groups. There was a certain kind of racial profiling that came with being a member of any specific tribe.<br /> <br /> But now, that cultural identity has been done away with, and the tribes are presented more like a bunch of gangs with shared political ideologies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-22T14:25:26-08:00","id":1558459,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the double post, the site seems to be bugging out when I try to quote multiple people.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558449#post1558449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not so much since Revised. A lot of names from Norse/Germanic myths still get used, but the later tribebook had them be defined more as the tribe that celebrates and obsesses over hypercompetence and stoicism. Part of that arguably makes them closer to modern US culture, and in particular some bits of the USMC. Kind of a funny reversal, as the Revised tribebook was written by an actual Scandanavian author and the typical accusations that the WoD focuses too much on the USA.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Probably because they weren't very knowledgeable about other regions. Didn't the Kuei Jin book have a section where the writers explicitly stated they didn't know anything about eastern culture, and told the players to just have fun?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558449#post1558449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Always true, but we have been ruminating over that since James Sembrano's Patreon posts revealed the reason why being completely and utterly metatextual (i.e. the creative director). Now, apparently European LARPs are a bit of a different deal and you might actually see racist Odinists about, as attested by some of the European members of the forums, but the Revised tribebook should have been license to shoot that dead on sight, since someone who reveres Odin would probably have been torn apart by the Get before they got anywhere near a rite of passage. The tribe does regard him as sworn enemy number one behind the direct forces of the Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They've spent centuries scouring the Umbra, looking for Odin, only to come home and find out he's been chilling in their grand mead hall this entire time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-22T15:42:05-08:00","id":1558460,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558457#post1558457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like Werewolf Fifth Edition made things a lot worse for the Garou Nation than they had been in any of the previous editions, especially the Twentieth Anniversary one, which was relatively optimistic by comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div>Contast that to BNS nearly all the cearns in at least north america was blown up by an apcolypise, the rites needed to make new ones are basically just bane magnets and king Albrecht sacrificed him self along with the silver crown so things don't get worse yet the nation is somehow still intact. Even more Politically split now but still intact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558458#post1558458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're sort of right.<br /> <br /> Pre-W5, the tribes were predominantly based around specific cultures or ethnic groups. There was a certain kind of racial profiling that came with being a member of any specific tribe.<br /> <br /> But now, that cultural identity has been done away with, and the tribes are presented more like a bunch of gangs with shared political ideologies.</div> </div> </div> </div>To quot a post I found on tumblur summed it up well:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/809289781747023872/sirobvious-sirobvious-appeal-to-a-wider?source=share\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://64.media.tumblr.com/32f919751a5e648b62ffea9c27ac3d7b/f53235cd1dec27b1-4c/s200x200u_c1/2d07ac9a08ce89b614aee31817ae3f2c188f6102.pnj\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/809289781747023872/sirobvious-sirobvious-appeal-to-a-wider?source=share\" target=\"_blank\"> Reblog by @songoftrillium </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/809289781747023872/sirobvious-sirobvious-appeal-to-a-wider?source=share\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/809289781747023872/sirobvious-sirobvious-appeal-to-a-wider?source=share </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> \ud83d\udcac 86&nbsp;&nbsp;\ud83d\udd01 100283&nbsp;&nbsp;\u2764\ufe0f 108027&nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;&ldquo;Appeal to a wider audience&rdquo; is corporate lingo for &ldquo;strip more themes from a piece of media so it&rsquo;s safer and more sanitized for investors&rdquo; </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201cAppeal to a wider audience\u201d is corporate lingo for \u201cstrip more themes from a piece of media so it\u2019s safer and more sanitized for investors\u201d<br /> <br /> I struck a nerve in the billionaire fandom with this one </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-22T17:34:57-08:00","id":1558461,"title":"","content":"Revised and W20 heavily downplayed a lot of ethnic membership stats. Some of the Revised tribebooks were a bit slow to it and wrote in ethnicity requirements into Pure Breed, but for example, even the GoF TB restrains itself from laying down a complete absolute, mentioning only that they're more commonly European. Given that PB is really more like a family legacy in a tribe than anything having to do with human bloodlines as such, it tracks; elsewhere in the tribebook, it also mentions that the Fenrir come from a wide variety of ethnic backgrounds. There's even a sidebar on page 20 to emphasize, again, that they're trying to shake off this &quot;Viking werewolves&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558459#post1558459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably because they weren't very knowledgeable about other regions. Didn't the Kuei Jin book have a section where the writers explicitly stated they didn't know anything about eastern culture, and told the players to just have fun?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not explicitly. That was what one can probably take from using the word &quot;exotic&quot; at every opportunity, as well as the atrocious handling of Chinese Romanization (Did Chi'uh Muh shake you? There is so much worse in store). I've never seen something more confidently wrong than the language sidebar in Blood and Silk.<br /> <br /> More to the point, GoF Revised was a purpose-built anti-myth. I recall a reviewer for the ancient Shadowessence forums getting tied up in a knot about that, decrying its take on Norse and Germanic myths as wrong, saying that there were elementary things that were backward, but it was all quite deliberate and informed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They've spent centuries scouring the Umbra, looking for Odin, only to come home and find out he's been chilling in their grand mead hall this entire time. </div> </div> </div>No, the ruination of Heimhalla was in the backstory of the tribe even further back than that. Wotan hides from them, now, for unlike their patron and ancestor they have many different pairs of eyes, noses, and sets of legs with which to wander. Also, given his association with death, it'd probably be in the Underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-22T21:58:44-08:00","id":1558462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558461#post1558461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's even a sidebar on page 20 to emphasize, again, that they're trying to shake off this &quot;Viking werewolves&quot; thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why the hell would anybody wanna do that!?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PgNxUMlDMAg\" data-code=\"PgNxUMlDMAg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/PgNxUMlDMAg/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-22T22:06:47-08:00","id":1558463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558460#post1558460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Contast that to BNS nearly all the cearns in at least north america was blown up by an apcolypise, the rites needed to make new ones are basically just bane magnets and king Albrecht sacrificed him self along with the silver crown so things don't get worse yet the nation is somehow still intact. Even more Politically split now but still intact.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm presuming that W5 changed the power dynamic with their reboot. But prior to 5th edition, the most powerful werewolf who was currently active in the physical world was the leader of the Black Spiral Dancers.<br /> <br /> Apparently, she was strong enough to solo entire packs of Garou and come out the victor.<br /> <br /> However, the most powerful werewolf in the WoD cosmology was Fenris. But after Odin trapped him inside the Umbra, he became severely limited in how much aid he was able to provide, until finally escaping during the apocalypse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-23T03:59:36-08:00","id":1558465,"title":"","content":"<br /> A bit off-topic, but it was always amusing how the Fenris even managed to survive considering their original tribal homeland, Heimhalla - originally the Jotunn kingdom of Utg\u00e5rd - was in a valley high in the mountains that separate Siberia from the lands towards the seas and Asia from Europe, the Ural Mountains<br /> <br /> Now this place was especially in a bad spot, stuck between the domain of Baba Yaga and the Empire of Odin that stretched from Germania to Russia - but originally (so they say) Odin/Wotan came from Asia<br /> <br /> Soo... Odin, the All-High, the Gangrel Methuselah and Wotan/Odin are one and the same?<br /> <br /> Good question, but it is not hat impossible, since it would fit the All-High's story and Dobrul the Brave, another alleged child of Ennoia is also from the East, from Mongolia<br /> Baba Yaga is a well known monster of the night and she was quite active in that age too<br /> <br /> So the young tribe was literally stuck between the Iron Hag (and the Little Grandmother had a plathora of nasty skills and servants to make the neighboring Lupine's life a living nightmare - especially since the Vo'lag - also known as Fomorians, Jotunn - the ancient race of giants in the service of the Wyrm dwelled in the northern hemisphere too and their little private wars with the Garou - mostly the Garou who later became or alredy been the Get of Fenris, the Fianna, White Howlers and the Wendigo - with drove them into the polar regions, right into her domain. And while the Jotunn retreted later into the Umbra in exile waiting for the Apocalypse I think it is logical they found an unexpected ally in the form of that ancient monstorsity) and between Odin, first from East, where he is originally from according their legends - and those legends probably exist becase Odin on his way to the West left a mark on their oral history - then from west, as he relocated his forces and empire and waged wars<br /> <br /> While we are here, it is worth to mention everything the Gangrel (or something like a a Gangrel) did actually fits quite nicely with the abilites of Odin/Woten of the Fenris; necromancy, warrior, God-like, blood magic that is so ancient a few even remember existed\u2026 and Fenris threw a mountainside on his enemy and crushed him, but lets be real, tanking a boulder half a size of a mountain is not that hard when you have things like protean, fortitude, necromancy and blood sorcery (especially the blood sorcery of the runic kind he used). And of course even the Fenris belive he survived and fled, tho' according them, in spirit<br /> Now around the same time the All-High, who was old when he arrived to the North apeared then moved into Uppsala, where he was worshipped as a living god, while he inspired strife among the various shapechangers of the North in order to strengthen his grip on its inhabitants. He travelled extensively across Scandinavia, Embracing various childer who later formed his Valkyries, those who searched for heroes and brought them to his temple to serve as ghouls. He used these warriors against the Get of Fenris in the Fenrir Wars.<br /> Nowdays he lies in torpor somewhere in Sweden, waiting for Gehenna.<br /> <br /> But to be fair, - and it is my personal headcanon - I think those Vampires from that time and that area managed to ascend a bit their undead status or may not been Gangrel at all<br /> Ravana became a Yama King<br /> Dobrul became something akin to a demigod who, according their own legends was respahed into a powerful Methuselah by a Wan Kuei Shaman's curse and Mother It\u00fcgen, the earth goddess embrace as he sank into the earth after the said shaman threw a great fireball to strike him\u2026 and eversince he was a thorn in the Keui-jin's side<br /> <br /> Odin became something like a Death-God, the Fenris called him &quot;the Gallow-God of the Aesir&quot;\u2026 or like Dobrul was something else; the Verbena believe the Wyck were the ones worshipped as godes like the Aesir, Vanir, and Tuatha De Danan and honestly the Get of Fenris Odin sounds more like a Wyck than a Methuselah who after Fenris flattened him with a mountain fled to become an undead and reworked his magic as runic and blood sorcery<br /> <br /> Or since that part of the World is a bit mellable what is in the Middle Kingdom and what is not in a given time, gathering enough power like Mikaboshi did or simply channeling the Faith and belife of Humans to <i>become something else</i> like Emma-O?<br /> <br /> It is a bit smiliar with Baba Yaga to be honest; Mongolia was/is part of the Middle Kingdom and before his demise the Yama King Dokhor-Khan, ruler of the Hell of Spiked Chains, claimed the souls of mortals that had died in the steppes Russia... is huge<br /> Half of Russia basically, the once Mongol territories and Siberia are in North Asia - it IS North Asia! Baba Yaga's Domain may not reached those areas (who knows?) but her influence and shadow certanly made the Kuei-jin Courts stirred<br /> Clearly Baba Yaga was old enough to see maybe the fall of the Wan Xian and her magic was tied to her Land - not unlike Koldunism, she was a shaman<br /> As a side note, the Spirit of the Living Earth is a heretical Dharma of the Kuei-jin that emphasizes both Yin and Yang. The Spirit of the Living Earth holds that creation itself is a spiritual entity compromised of various other smaller spirits that exist everywhere around in the Material World within their own realms. The material world itself is a vaporous illusion, one that parts to reveal the true power of spirit beyond. Only by propitiating these spirits can one expect their aid and compliance, and eventually, enlightenment and salvation by turning into a spirit themselves.<br /> The Spirit of the Living Earth has been labelled heretic because they have no qualms about trafficking with demons and other tainted spirits- as they are still spirits.<br /> <br /> The are for all thense and propsues are Shamans or very animistic at least Baba Yaga and her quasi-koldunism after her Embrace was clearly stirred the Spirits - both the Yang and Yin worlds and she summoned the Zmei ; they were once mighty servants of the Wyld who were corrupted by the power of the Wyrm. In ancient nights, their corrupted selves were brought into the world by Baba Yaga in an attempt to kill the Nosferatu Antediluvian.<br /> Before their fall they were even possible Yang Dragons or lesser ministers of Heaven and she also summoned Koshchei, the First Finger, one of the Talons of the Wyrm - the Wyrm is known to the Kuei-Jin and the Hengeyokai they call it Lord Centipede who wants to knock the Wheel of Ages off of its hinges entirely, meaning that it's up to the Changing Breeds AND the Kuei-jin to prevent this from occurring - both parties main tenet is the Wheel MUST turn.<br /> In this case theTalons of the Wyrm would be the &quot;legs of Lord Centipede&quot; maybe (they based it probably on \u014cmukade, a giant man-eating centipede Yokai that lives in the mountains. While it eats humans, it also preys on great serpents and dragons.) the tallons of Lord Centipede - \u014cmukade in some depictions have hands and claws.<br /> Baba Yaga and her magic tied to the Land this to the Ley lines/Dragon lines and Caerns/Dragon Nests - both yin and yang ones and effected the Yang and Yin Realms, and even Yomi to a degree.<br /> It is possible or likely Baba Yaga became a Yama Queen after her demise/ascendence<br /> <br /> Her domain was criss-crossed with Lay Lines/Dragon Lines, she was a Shaman and her might was so great she pulled such entites as the Zmei and Kochei in to the Material World/Middle Kingdom and her domain was partially if not entirely part of &quot;area of influence&quot; of Dokhor-Khan, ruler of the Hell of Spiked Chains, claimed the souls of mortals that had died in the steppes (After the creation of the Quincunx, around the end of the 12 century, the Kuei-jin attacked the holdings of Dokhor-Khan in the former territories of the Black Tortoise Court, severing him from his input of Tainted Chi, which allowed his rivals, among them Rangda and Tou Mu, to destroy him and add parts of the former Hell to their own territories)<br /> With such geographical and spiritual background it is possible she &quot;Ascended&quot; and craved out a Yama Hell of her own in Yomi<br /> She woldn't be the first Cainite whe ascended to Demonhood<br /> Ravana aside there is Cybele who became a Decani, Another Decani, Anoster was replaced by Mary the Black in the 18th century, Nergal was described to be effectively a demon in a vampire's body, and Beckett's Jyhad Diary basically confirmed he became one and Chaining the Beast mentions Nahema, the younger sister of the Twins Arikel and Malkav who descended into Hell, but never lost touch with her siblings, her spirit forever bound to them and their childer \u2013 it is Nahema's spirit that whispers in the Malkavian Madness Network, that burns in the hearts of the Toreador. Some of her worshippers call her the Dark Muse, the Anti-Muse, and the Demon Queen of Madness, and she is said to be patron saint of serial killers and torturers<br /> <br /> Baba Yaga was <i>Cruel</i>\u2026. yet strangely maternal \u2014 she punished but rarely harmed the truly innocent. She retained her folkloric cunning and sense of justice toward the land and spirits.<br /> In Baba Yaga's case everythgin was given to become something more after her Final Death - what may not be that final at all, since quite a few sources describes the echos and shadows of her rule still lingering around\u2026<br /> <br /> Now, back to the original train of thought, stuck between whatever Odin was (or is) and Baba Yaga, not to mention the Shadow Lord's as neighbors with their own problem with Kupala and the Eldest, it is a minor miracle the Fenris survived and managed to became a Tribe at all even if the moved westward to the Skandinavia area (probably pursuing Odin...)!<br /> <br /> (And frankly these are not &quot;damnable crossover things&quot;, they are, Baba Yaga, Odin, Kupala and the Tzimsice, the whole enchilada are part of the Werewolf line - but expanded in their own seperate lines, thats true)<br /> <br /> But back to the original original question... this complexity and ritch background you can dig up and mix and mingle what is was lost betwee nthre editions and made the whole Garou Nation worse or basically nonexistant at all","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 02-24-2026, 02:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-23T04:49:02-08:00","id":1558466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558465#post1558465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Now, back to the original train of thought, stuck between whatever Odin was (or is) and Baba Yaga, not to mention the Shadow Lord's as neighbors with their own problem with Kupala and the Eldest, it is a minor miracle the Fenris survived and managed to became a Tribe at all even if the moved westward to the Skandinavia area (probably pursuing Odin...)!<br /> <br /> (And frankly these are not &quot;damnable crossover things&quot;, they are, Baba Yaga, Odin, Kupala and the Tzimsice, the whole enchilada are part of the Werewolf line - but expanded in their own seperate lines, thats true)<br /> <br /> But back to the original original question... this complexity and ritch background you can dig up and mix and mingle what is was lost betwee nthre editions and made the whole Garou Nation worse or basically nonexistant at all</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so much of a miracle. As I said previously, Fenris is the most powerful werewolf in the original World of Darkness cosmology. Past, present or future, there will not be any other Garou stronger than him; and he heavily encouraged his tribe to follow his example. The Get of Fenris were not just warriors, they were THE preeminent warriors of the Garou Nation.<br /> <br /> <br /> Bare in mind that it takes an Elder vampire to have a realistic chance of defeating a Garou in combat, and the Garou like to operate in packs. Meaning that although you did list some pretty heavy hitters, they were going up against the mightiest tribe of badasses the Garo Nation had to offer.<br /> <br /> <br /> While every other tribe seems to be consistently getting their asses kicked by the changes that took place throughout history, the Get of Fenris were still wracking up victories.<br /> <br /> --------------------<br /> <br /> Yes, the Black Furies may have stopped them from invading their caern in the ancient past, but they accomplished that by shutting down the Moon Bridges while the Get were still in transit. Causing them to either drop out of the sky, or get trapped in whatever pocket dimension they were traveling through at the time.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, the Windego may have fought the Get to a draw back in ancient times. But that was then, and this is now; oh, how the mighty have fallen!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 02-23-2026, 07:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-23T07:30:45-08:00","id":1558468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558462#post1558462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Why the hell would anybody wanna do that!?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it's a shallow pool and you'll break your neck diving in. Also, because it's respect for history - vikings weren't a super warrior culture, but rather villagers who engaged in piracy in less favorable times, and then sold off their plunder to cement their wealth. Get believe in fighting for its own sake, so they're not exactly going to meet in the middle . Well, unless it's to tear them apart for revering the Aesir and Vanir, anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm presuming that W5 changed the power dynamic with their reboot. But prior to 5th edition, the most powerful werewolf who was currently active in the physical world was the leader of the Black Spiral Dancers. </div> </div> </div>Nope. She was tied with Golgol Fangs-First. Also, to put aside the paper tiger of stats alone for a second, Silver Fangs can turn into silver, which... well, she wouldn't last long against Luna's Avenger, extra dots of physicals or not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Apparently, she was strong enough to solo entire packs of Garou and come out the victor. </div> </div> </div>Heavily hinted to be some kind of fate-warping on the part of one of her packmates if she managed to accomplish that. After he died, though, so did the prophecy. Her plot armor crumbled with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, the most powerful werewolf in the WoD cosmology was Fenris. But after Odin trapped him inside the Umbra, he became severely limited in how much aid he was able to provide, until finally escaping during the apocalypse. </div> </div> </div>Being an Incarna expressly keeps one from being able to be considered a werewolf, and as far as the line presents it, Fenris was always an Incarna of battle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While every other tribe seems to be consistently getting their asses kicked by the changes that took place throughout history, the Get of Fenris were still wracking up victories. </div> </div> </div>The Sept of the Bloodfist suffered a near-total attrition between 1993 and 2001. Only one of the Garou from Caerns: Places of Power was still alive to get mentioned in A World of Rage. Not exactly a great big W if you get maimed so badly you can't really hold one of your foremost caerns anymore. In this, the Get suffer from the Spartan Problem, of overextending themselves and then not being able to reliably defend territory - a truly dramatic sort of irony, given their want to pick fights and &quot;aggressively defend&quot; the caerns of others when their numbers dipped.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Baba Yaga was <i>Cruel</i>\u2026. yet strangely maternal \u2014 she punished but rarely harmed the truly innocent.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Given their stated rarity... how would you really be able to tell? You'd have to see some truly strange stars align correctly to be present for when that happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-23T10:32:01-08:00","id":1558472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558468#post1558468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope. She was tied with Golgol Fangs-First. Also, to put aside the paper tiger of stats alone for a second, Silver Fangs can turn into silver, which... well, she wouldn't last long against Luna's Avenger, extra dots of physicals or not.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Gogol is the guy dual wielding miniguns in the Amazon rainforest, isn't he?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558468#post1558468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because it's a shallow pool and you'll break your neck diving in. Also, because it's respect for history - vikings weren't a super warrior culture, but rather villagers who engaged in piracy in less favorable times, and then sold off their plunder to cement their wealth. Get believe in fighting for its own sake, so they're not exactly going to meet in the middle . Well, unless it's to tear them apart for revering the Aesir and Vanir, anyway.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, selecting the best warriors on the battlefield, to join your army in the afterlife as you train them to fight giants (Jotuns) at the literal end of the world is the entire premise behind Valhalla and Ragnarok.<br /> <br /> <b>Fun Fact:</b> Even in real life mythology, Odin was fated to be slain by Fenrir.<br /> <br /> Though sadly for the big doggo, he is killed shortly after by Vidar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-23T19:50:04-08:00","id":1558478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558472#post1558472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Gogol is the guy dual wielding miniguns in the Amazon rainforest, isn't he?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think that was just a piece that had an art direction note of &quot;like the Predator, but even more metal&quot;. Golgol has actual portraits in the books where he appears, though the one in RAtA is less detailed than his card art from Rage or the one in GoF Revised (where he looks like he's been in the fight about two or three times longer than the Amazon War proper lasted, with a multitude of extra battle scars and no hair).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, selecting the best warriors on the battlefield, to join your army in the afterlife as you train them to fight giants (Jotuns) at the literal end of the world is the entire premise behind Valhalla and Ragnarok. </div> </div> </div>An ideal. Humans are historically bad at living up to those in the face of practicality. Also, the idealized top of the heap wouldn't get anywhere without the navigators, or still afford boats without the merchant side of the culture.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Fun Fact:</b> Even in real life mythology, Odin was fated to be slain by Fenrir.<br /> <br /> Though sadly for the big doggo, he is killed shortly after by Vidar. </div> </div> </div>Everyone dies in that story. It's the Twilight of the Gods. Which Christian missionaries then spun as having already happened to get everyone on board with their &quot;sequel&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-23T22:06:49-08:00","id":1558480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558478#post1558478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An ideal. Humans are historically bad at living up to those in the face of practicality. Also, the idealized top of the heap wouldn't get anywhere without the navigators, or still afford boats without the merchant side of the culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what magic is for. We call it mythology today, but back in those times, they were full fledged religions. You don't perform ritualistic human sacrifices on a routine basis, unless you genuinely expect to get something out of it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558478#post1558478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Everyone dies in that story. It's the Twilight of the Gods. Which Christian missionaries then spun as having already happened to get everyone on board with their &quot;sequel&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not everyone. At least 2 of the pantheon survive Ragnarok by hiding inside Yggdrasil, then their descendants repopulate the next world.<br /> <br /> Hela's ultimate fate is also not specified, so there's a chance she could still be around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-24T12:20:52-08:00","id":1558495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558480#post1558480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's what magic is for. We call it mythology today, but back in those times, they were full fledged religions. You don't perform ritualistic human sacrifices on a routine basis, unless you genuinely expect to get something out of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That just makes it even more likely that the only Get involved with Viking culture would be Ragabash on infiltration missions! Everyone else would be busy trying to stamp out the unclean spirits welcomed in by Vikings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not everyone. At least 2 of the pantheon survive Ragnarok by hiding inside Yggdrasil, then their descendants repopulate the next world.<br /> <br /> Hela's ultimate fate is also not specified, so there's a chance she could still be around. </div> </div> </div>I do keep forgetting how readily it dovetails into the sequel pitch that Christianity pulled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude18","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-24T14:33:12-08:00","id":1558498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558495#post1558495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That just makes it even more likely that the only Get involved with Viking culture would be Ragabash on infiltration missions! Everyone else would be busy trying to stamp out the unclean spirits welcomed in by Vikings.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I do keep forgetting how readily it dovetails into the sequel pitch that Christianity pulled.</div> </div> </div> </div>The real tragedy is that the beef with Fenrir was entirely avoidable.<br /> <br /> Fenrir wanted to be friends with the gods, but Odin had a nightmare about a big, scary wolf and assumed it must have been a prophetic warning.<br /> <br /> Fenrir, still being a puppy at the time, thought their attempts to bind him were just a game. So when they finally succeeded and left him on the side of the road, he swore vengeance, thus creating the very threat Odin was trying to prevent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-24T16:10:22-08:00","id":1558500,"title":"","content":"Well on the topic of Fenrir one W5 Homebrew I saw that attempted to tie it into legacy is that Fenrir was accidentally banished into the deep umbra by a &quot;dooms day rite&quot; that's meant to to cut the Wyrm off from completely taking over the umbra. <br /> <br /> He was recovered some time later by by the Get (who took Wild fire as a temporary patron in the intrem) but the whole experience give him turbo PTSD and subsequently infected his whole tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-24T16:21:18-08:00","id":1558502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558500#post1558500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well on the topic of Fenrir one W5 Homebrew I saw that attempted to tie it into legacy is that Fenrir was accidentally banished into the deep umbra by a &quot;dooms day rite&quot; that's meant to to cut the Wyrm off from completely taking over the umbra.<br /> <br /> He was recovered some time later by by the Get (who took Wild fire as a temporary patron in the intrem) but the whole experience give him turbo PTSD and subsequently infected his whole tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fenrir does not get PTSD!<br /> <br /> People get PTSD from Fenrir!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-24T16:48:44-08:00","id":1558503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558498#post1558498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The real tragedy is that the beef with Fenrir was entirely avoidable.<br /> <br /> Fenrir wanted to be friends with the gods, but Odin had a nightmare about a big, scary wolf and assumed it must have been a prophetic warning.<br /> <br /> Fenrir, still being a puppy at the time, thought their attempts to bind him were just a game. So when they finally succeeded and left him on the side of the road, he swore vengeance, thus creating the very threat Odin was trying to prevent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though if we're talking WoD, Fenrir was never a puppy, what with being an Incarna and all. Also, not one of Loki's kids, explained in the tribebook as humans hearing &quot;Loki conjured an image of Fenrir to show Wotan&quot; and wildly misinterpreting it.<br /> <br /> (Tyr got the short end of the stick in both cases.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-24T23:03:38-08:00","id":1558507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558503#post1558503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Though if we're talking WoD, Fenrir was never a puppy, what with being an Incarna and all. Also, not one of Loki's kids, explained in the tribebook as humans hearing &quot;Loki conjured an image of Fenrir to show Wotan&quot; and wildly misinterpreting it.<br /> <br /> (Tyr got the short end of the stick in both cases.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Crucified himself for two weeks to gain insight, but also received crippling paranoia in the process.<br /> <br /> What a rip off!<br /> <br /> ((In hindsight, Ragnarok seems like a self fulfilling prophecy, actually. Many of the threats and problems were directly caused by Odin trying to avoid them))","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 02-25-2026, 02:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-25T19:25:36-08:00","id":1558520,"title":"","content":"I would like to cycle back to cover a few points in the OP that I've been ruminating over.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off#post1558364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One complaint I'm seeing a lot of is that 5th Edition is much harder on the Garou and nothing but how much they suck.<br /> <br /> However, I remember 1st Edition Werewolf and early 2nd Edition. In fact, that's &quot;my&quot; W:TA because I didn't follow up on Revised and other works.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you were that familiar with it you'd also know that, being an early WoD first edition, it was 90% vibes being thrown at the wall to see what stuck. People tend to assemble these through rose-colored glasses, not unlike &quot;Only 3025&quot; BattleTech players. RIP to the suggested Superhero theme and play mode and Wolf-Headed Bikini Babes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The point was that the Garou had failed and the Apocalypse was imminent...because of all the reasons given in the 5th Edition book about them being too violent, unable to get over their differences tribally, and the Children of Gaia being ignored. It was why Evan-White-Boy-Saves-Us ( :kidding, kidding: ) existed as his whole thing. The Garou needed to make serious systemic change or everyone was screwed. </div> </div> </div>And 2e starting with Legacy Rite didn't suggest that they were doing something fairly different? 2e was also where the game declared its theme - Savage Horror, which the Storyteller's Handbook clarified was splatter. Gross-out horror. You were fighting Troma mutants and painting the walls with them before they painted the walls with you, not unlike Splatterhouse. And speaking of said Storyteller's Handbook, it was knee-deep in Joseph Campbell and applying mythic cycle storytelling to W:tA (also a thing that didn't exactly age well, much like the dedication to Neil Gaiman in the front of the 1e W:tA core).<br /> <br /> Also, both 1e and 2e had miniatures game rules in the back. Honestly, it's a wonder that Trinity: Battleground became WW's first hero-based miniatures combat game, because W:tA had a lot of potential in that arena.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not a big fan of 5E's take but I am curious why this specific complaint is coming up because it seems like it was just following up from the original presentation that all of the War of Rage, Impergium, and other things had come to roost.<br /> <br /> Change or die and all that.<br /> <br /> I wonder if this is related to the editions I missed and the fact that 5E was going back to the original versions. </div> </div> </div>5e is stripping things down just like it did to Vampire. If it had actually gone back to its roots, there would be more superheroic Garou and wolf-headed bikini babes. Instead, it's the flattening of everything into the One True Way, with a heavy serving of how the creative director hates the game, and also you for liking it, and the stunt-casted developer kind of agrees with him because it wasn't enough like Vampire. And the OTW here isn't splatter or a emphasis on the visceral and chilling nature of violence, but an attempt to force V:tM's standard of &quot;personal horror&quot; onto a setting that does not give a shit about it.<br /> <br /> That is the problem. Throwbacks to the 90s getting control, preaching about making a &quot;modern version&quot; of games, and engaging in finger-wagging about character optimization that wouldn't be out of place in a usenet post from 1993. It doesn't understand how the concept of Loresheets from Weapons of the Gods are supposed to work and wastes all potential that they would have. It doesn't even have time for consideration of wolves and wolf behavior, in a game where a notable character type is born as a wolf and lives as one for a (very harrowing and traumatizing) year or two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-25T21:10:55-08:00","id":1558521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558520#post1558520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5e is stripping things down just like it did to Vampire. If it had actually gone back to its roots, there would be more superheroic Garou and wolf-headed bikini babes. Instead, it's the flattening of everything into the One True Way, with a heavy serving of how the creative director hates the game, and also you for liking it, and the stunt-casted developer kind of agrees with him because it wasn't enough like Vampire. And the OTW here isn't splatter or a emphasis on the visceral and chilling nature of violence, but an attempt to force V:tM's standard of &quot;personal horror&quot; onto a setting that does not give a shit about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honstly As I said BNS and apparently the first version of W5 was going to be closer. where a apocalypse actually did happene but the old heroes of the garou has to commit to the ultimate sacrifice to ensure the world is intact for next generation. <br /> <br /> While nearly all the cearns was blown up in the process the nation still survives is still more politically divided. <br /> <br /> This is partly why some fans basically going to make they own WtA edition in all but name. They even got a former WtA writer on they team.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-26T10:58:44-08:00","id":1558529,"title":"","content":"As far as the &quot;back to the roots&quot;-argument for W5 is concerned, I never found that one to be plausible. There's way too much antipathy for Garou in this edition. In that regard, the pre-gen-characters in the adventures have been particularly illuminating. You often get the sense that in W5 the way a potential Garou-PC-concept works is to imagine a human who has some motivation to oppose the forces of the Wyrm - and then all the Garou/werewolf-stuff is just an afterthought. It's an extreme example but there's this one pre-gen-character in the adventures Crude Earth and Rotten Home that's a great example of just that:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Deputy Sheriff Maya Chamberlain (Humanborn Silver Fang Philodox): Raised by her grandmother in Mulligan, Maya has no other family in town. She also has an Iron-Clad sense of right and wrong that brooks little argument. Fortunately for the people who come through Mulligan, listening is high on her list of right, and jumping to conclusions is high on her list of wrong.<br /> She\u2019s currently not welcome on Caern grounds because when the elder put her in a situation of choosing between her job and the Caern, she chose her job as she believes losing her job would make the Caern less safe.\u200b </div> </div> </div>This one is quite extreme by highlighting the idea that when this character was in a situation where she had to choose between protecting the Caern and making sure she would keep her human job, she ended up choosing the latter. At that point, I honestly wonder why this character even should be a W5-PC. Just let her do her human job and help that way. Clearly, she thinks that's more important than being a Garou in a Pack that protects the local Caern.<br /> <br /> But if you read this backstory with the idea that she's right and the Garou at the local Caern are wrong, then you get an idea of what W5 considers to be a &quot;good Garou&quot;. What W5 imagines &quot;good Garou&quot; to do is to focus on establishing a balanced human life (job, family, money etc.) and you try to help the local Caern/Sept as much as possible. But the Garou who want you to treat being a Garou like a full-time-job and prioritize protecting the Caern and fighting the Wyrm are the bad guys. Furthermore, the mechanics of W5 support that idea. Going into the Umbra has been discouraged, shapeshifting is costly (especially the Crinos Form), Rage-management is hard (as in when you want to have a lot of dots and when you want to have few) and Harano/Hauglosk are these &quot;inevitable doom&quot;-mechanics.<br /> <br /> There's a section in the 1st edition WtA corebook in Chapter Three called &quot;Heroics&quot;. W5 is pretty much the antithesis of this idea. In 1st edition you would get a line from the Heroics-section like &quot;Stories in WtA should present the characters with the opportunity to be heroes. Through the characters players can right the wrongs they do not have the power to correct in real life.&quot; (pg. 63). I could quote more but you get the idea, it's a whole section about how thinking of the Garou as heroes is important in this 1st edition framework.<br /> <br /> Now let's see a section from the W5 corebook adding its thoughts on this subject: &quot;Note, too, that this difference means that the players\u2019 characters are the protagonists, but by no means are they the \u201cheroes\u201d or the \u201cgood guys.\u201d The Garou are, by definition, flawed individually, and Garou society is\u2026 well, it\u2019s a fucking trainwreck. The players\u2019 characters are agents of change, not necessarily improvement. The proof of the change they bring lies in the outcomes they effect. Werewolf assumes that most players\u2019 characters do seek some sort of improvement to the world, but the game doesn\u2019t insist on such linearity. Also, characters may be limited by their Garou nature or other things outside their control.\u200b&quot; The undertone of pessimism is pretty obvious, I think.<br /> <br /> I mean, what a contrast! First edition clearly had a setting in mind that's close to Apocalypse and a grimdark world but the PCs were meant to be heroes who struggled against it. In W5 meanwhile the writers are describing an apocalyptic setting and they've also already lost any faith in Garou (and the PCs must be Garou, of course) to make a difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-26T15:31:42-08:00","id":1558537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558529#post1558529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean this straight up sounds like Pentex propaganda. Hell it actually Echoes real life coprate propaganda attempts to try and deflect they responsibilities away from themselves and the systems they propped up and onto the indervidurals. <br /> <br /> like that why I'd think W5 is actually a matrix like situation with the players waiting to break out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-26T16:00:31-08:00","id":1558538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558521#post1558521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is partly why some fans basically going to make they own WtA edition in all but name. They even got a former WtA writer on they team.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Galliard Group actually did make their own 5th edition, which I think they jokingly refer to as 'Werewolf 3.5,' or something like that.<br /> <br /> The original plot for W5 actually sounds like it could have been halfway decent. A new Savage Age taking place in a post apocalyptic future would have been way more metal than this lukewarm version that tries to get us to sympathize with the fucking Fomori.<br /> <br /> -----------------<br /> <br /> Honestly, I'm surprised that W5 is trying to tone things down. Seeing as the last time they tried that with Forsaken, the guy they brought on to write Changing Breeds used the book as a giant middle finger to the company for removing the eco-terrorist aspect from the setting.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-26T17:12:07-08:00","id":1558539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558538#post1558538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly, I'm surprised that W5 is trying to tone things down. Seeing as the last time they tried that with Forsaken, the guy they brought on to write <b>Changing Breeds</b> used the book as a giant middle finger to the company for removing the eco-terrorist aspect from the setting.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>... Uh that is ... <i>a take</i> on changing breeds if I ever seen one. Like from what I've heard the whole book doubles down on the more iffy elements of wta and not really have the decency on being choeraint nor fun book to and play.<br /> <br /> Like my man there's already alienate take on that with <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rYxBILf2PLVVKgF07shwMY6z9_lIcUEEEfne7iiTV44/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Nagual : The Inginted</a>.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-26T18:12:54-08:00","id":1558540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558539#post1558539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... Uh that is ... <i>a take</i> on changing breeds if I ever seen one. Like from what I've heard the whole book doubles down on the more iffy elements of wta and not really have the decency on being choeraint nor fun book to and play.<br /> <br /> Like my man there's already alienate take on that with <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rYxBILf2PLVVKgF07shwMY6z9_lIcUEEEfne7iiTV44/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Nagual : The Inginted</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book had effectively ZERO communication going on between the people who worked on it. Like, right at the beginning, they tell you that the different changing breeds aren't restricted by ethnicity, but then when you get to the Wererat section, it explicitly states every single Wererat is from Indian stock.<br /> <br /> <br /> Wereelephants were so hideously over powered straight out of character creation, that even a human with 5 dots in all their physical attributes / skills had no chance of taking them down in combat.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Wererabbit was an especially huge disappointment, as the art for them was just a human with a single rabbit ear hanging over the side of their shoulder.<br /> <br /> <br /> Weregoats were described as being hermaphrodites who engage in satanic worship, which is very obviously a nod to Baphomet.<br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------------<br /> <br /> EDIT: As for it being a middle finger, I understand the lead writer hated how they removed the aspect of Garou being warriors of Gaia and instead became a bunch of mediators and wardens of the spirit world.<br /> <br /> So when it came to Changing Breeds, they heavily emphasized the part about humanity being evil, and how the shifters were fighting to protect nature. Instead of spirits, you've got artwork featuring them going after street criminals, poachers, human traffickers, est.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 02-26-2026, 09:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-26T18:59:03-08:00","id":1558541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558540#post1558540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> EDIT: As for it being a middle finger, I understand the lead writer hated how they removed the aspect of Garou being warriors of Gaia and instead became a bunch of mediators and wardens of the spirit world.<br /> <br /> So when it came to Changing Breeds, they heavily emphasized the part about humanity being evil, and how the shifters were fighting to protect nature. Instead of spirits, you've got artwork featuring them going after street criminals, poachers, human traffickers, est.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well you cant really accuse Forsaken especially 2e of lacking a solid vision unlike W5. The devs has gone out of they way of to make setting distinct from apocalypse and they argubly succeeded. to the point that arguably did some of the stuff W5 did better. Like compare the W5 in contrast to the Forsaken tribes and the many lodges that makes up the tribe or the deep bloody history on why the pure and the forsaken conflict through out the ages in contrasts to the cult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 02-26-2026, 10:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-26T19:06:10-08:00","id":1558542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558540#post1558540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The book had effectively ZERO communication going on between the people who worked on it. Like, right at the beginning, they tell you that the different changing breeds aren't restricted by ethnicity, but then when you get to the Wererat section, it explicitly states every single Wererat is from Indian stock.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't recall, and probably do not wish to, if there was a lot of room open for alternate types of changing breeds of the same animal, so I can't recall if it was just that type of wererat or intended to be all wererats everywhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wereelephants were so hideously over powered straight out of character creation, that even a human with 5 dots in all their physical attributes / skills had no chance of taking them down in combat. </div> </div> </div>You think that the elephants were overpowered? This was a Satyr Brucato joint. The weretigers had more powerful war forms and more Dex on top of that. Never underestimate his capacity to overstat cats.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Wererabbit was an especially huge disappointment, as the art for them was just a human with a single rabbit ear hanging over the side of their shoulder.<br /> <br /> <br /> Weregoats were described as being hermaphrodites who engage in satanic worship, which is very obviously a nod to Baphomet.<br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------------<br /> <br /> EDIT: As for it being a middle finger, I understand the lead writer hated how they removed the aspect of Garou being warriors of Gaia and instead became a bunch of mediators and wardens of the spirit world.<br /> <br /> So when it came to Changing Breeds, they heavily emphasized the part about humanity being evil, and how the shifters were fighting to protect nature. Instead of spirits, you've got artwork featuring them going after street criminals, poachers, human traffickers, est. </div> </div> </div>I haven't heard much of anything from him except details about M20, so I can't say. I do know that the Bubasti literally got copypasted into that book almost unchanged from Bastet. The only change was that there were a lot more of them because like the Tremere, they had a fully-fledged...<br /> <br /> (SUNGLASSES ON)<br /> <br /> Pyramid structure.<br /> <br /> meetthenewboss.mp3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-26T19:20:57-08:00","id":1558544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558542#post1558542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You think that the elephants were overpowered? This was a Satyr Brucato joint. The weretigers had more powerful war forms and more Dex on top of that. Never underestimate his capacity to overstat cats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yes, I had heard they had a rather unhealthy obsession with felines, as evidenced by how they would wax poetically about how beautiful and perfect they were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-01T06:11:58-08:00","id":1558567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558538#post1558538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The original plot for W5 actually sounds like it could have been halfway decent. A new Savage Age taking place in a post apocalyptic future would have been way more metal than this lukewarm version that tries to get us to sympathize with the fucking Fomori.</div> </div> </div> </div>When W5's key-terms are things like &quot;The Garou Nation has fallen&quot;, &quot;Gaia's dead/dying&quot; and &quot;Age of Apocalypse&quot;, it does feel like a natural conclusion to think of a post-apocalyptic setting. Especially coupled with the corebook's pessimistic opinion on Garou in general. <br /> <br /> But there are two sections in the book that I think describe well what the game aims for:<br /> <br /> There's a bit on caerns and the players' Pack on pg. 191:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As a game, Werewolf: The Apocalypse assumes that the players\u2019 characters will have their own caern, or that their pack will belong to the sept of a specific caern. </div> </div> </div>So you already got the assumption that you're gonna be tied to a caern. And then there's a section concerning the usual scope of W5 games on pg. 212:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The other axis is that of systemic / individual. Systemic antagonists are large, overarching entities or ideals. Systemic antagonists are massive and often decentralized and, in general, cannot be directly defeated. They can certainly face setbacks at the hands of the characters, but total defeat is almost never an option. Most systemic antagonists have local proxies that can be defeated, thereby hurting the global antagonist\u2019s plans and relieving tension \u2014 the \u201clittle victories\u201d that mean so much in Werewolf, because they address the player characters\u2019 immediate goals. The Wyrm is one of the best examples of a systemic antagonist, as is Pentex Group. </div> </div> </div>And there you have your &quot;street-level only&quot;-perspective by saying that it's all just about these &quot;little victories&quot;. And so far, the kind of adventures that have been put out by Renegade can be sorted into two categories. The first one is &quot;Small town, humans doing bad stuff and... would you look at that! It turns out the people in charge are Fomori!&quot;. This is all the Pentex-related stuff or some people just doing some bad stuff to the environment, other people and whatever. And the second one is &quot;Hey, there's some other Garou over there... hang on a sec... They're Bad Guys!&quot;. And the second one is where you get Cult of Fenris, Black Spiral Dancers and the like.<br /> <br /> There are two that stand out, though, for being particularly weird in my opinion. <br /> <br /> The first one is the last adventure in the Scent Of Decay book with the rival Pack. Because that's about a Gaia-loyal Pack that has pledged itself to the Horned Serpent Tribal Patron Spirit. They're on a mission to deliberately let a small town fall to the Wyrm to study it, though. And the Horned Serpent supports them. This, it turns out, brings the Players' Pack into conflict with them because they want to stop the forces of the Wyrm in that small town. Very weird take on a Pack loyal to the Horned Serpent. Also it made me laugh that at one point, you encounter the Horned Serpent with the rival Pack present and the Horned Serpent is like &quot;I want to hear both Packs about what they did and why.&quot; So you make your case and the rival Pack make their case for why they're right but then the Horned Serpent is like &quot;Hmm, I've changed my mind. Whoever can recruit this one person who's a Kin first will get my support.&quot;<br /> <br /> The second one is &quot;Rotten Home&quot;. The players' Pack is sent by their Sept to another one in order to build an alliance. The PCs get there and the Sept feels like a cult. Then you're asked to join a Legendary Rite that is all about telling the story of how the Weaver corrupted the Wyrm and that's what led to the dismal state of the world. Then the leader of the Sept tries to explain that fighting against the Weaver is more important than fighting against the Wyrm. Then the adventure essentially concludes with the players supposedly having to take a stance on this. One of the options is to actually start a debate over which one is worse, the Weaver or the Wyrm? According to the adventure, you have this evil heretic with evil ambitions... but all that's going on is there's just some creepy dude who wants to sell you on his elevator-pitch for what he calls &quot;A really cool idea&quot;. And you can beat the crap out of him if you don't like his elevator-pitch. Thought that was a weird adventure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-01T14:57:51-08:00","id":1558577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558567#post1558567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When W5's key-terms are things like &quot;The Garou Nation has fallen&quot;, &quot;Gaia's dead/dying&quot; and &quot;Age of Apocalypse&quot;, it does feel like a natural conclusion to think of a post-apocalyptic setting. Especially coupled with the corebook's pessimistic opinion on Garou in general.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It would also give the other Fera more of a chance to shine, and demonstrate just how badly flawed the Garou were.<br /> <br /> Rokea were specifically tasked with surviving the Apocalypse and helping to repopulate the world after it's passing. This means that Gaia foresaw the Garou would lose the war, and made a contingency for just such an occasion.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Kitsune were promised to not only survive the Apocalypse, but that they would also be granted a purpose once it was all set and done. A post apocalyptic setting would have been a great way to introduce that, instead of having them sit around in Asia waiting for Gaia to give them orders.<br /> <br /> <br /> Then we've got the Makole, who's ability to tap into the memories of the entire planet would have been great way to ensure that people in that setting avoid repeating the mistakes of the past and work towards establishing a better future. <i>&quot;Don't be a raging maniac, and don't allow corporate greed to blind you to the planet's suffering.&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-01T15:36:52-08:00","id":1558578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558567#post1558567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When W5's key-terms are things like &quot;The Garou Nation has fallen&quot;, &quot;Gaia's dead/dying&quot; and &quot;Age of Apocalypse&quot;, it does feel like a natural conclusion to think of a post-apocalyptic setting. Especially coupled with the corebook's pessimistic opinion on Garou in general.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Again in BNS nearly all the cearns was blown up by the Apocalypse but the nation still stands.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So you already got the assumption that you're gonna be tied to a caern. And then there's a section concerning the usual scope of W5 games on pg. 212: </div> </div> </div>On the subject of caerns, reclaiming them is going to be a main focus for the BNS version from what little I've read. Either as a reward for the players efforts for securing a area or it's going to be a focus of a episodic campaign where players go around amerca helping isolated septs reclaim they cearns. Which is a step up from what W is offering narrative wise since all the Small victories might actually contribute larger victory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> According to the adventure, you have this evil heretic with evil ambitions... but all that's going on is there's just some creepy dude who wants to sell you on his elevator-pitch for what he calls &quot;A really cool idea&quot;. And you can beat the crap out of him if you don't like his elevator-pitch. Thought that was a weird adventure. </div> </div> </div>Well evil guy that might have a point is a oddly prevalent trope in current left presenting media land scape.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558577#post1558577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would also give the other Fera more of a chance to shine, and demonstrate just how badly flawed the Garou were.<br /> <br /> Rokea were specifically tasked with surviving the Apocalypse and helping to repopulate the world after it's passing. This means that Gaia foresaw the Garou would lose the war, and made a contingency for just such an occasion.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Kitsune were promised to not only survive the Apocalypse, but that they would also be granted a purpose once it was all set and done. A post apocalyptic setting would have been a great way to introduce that, instead of having them sit around in Asia waiting for Gaia to give them orders.<br /> <br /> <br /> Then we've got the Makole, who's ability to tap into the memories of the entire planet would have been great way to ensure that people in that setting avoid repeating the mistakes of the past and work towards establishing a better future. <i>&quot;Don't be a raging maniac, and don't allow corporate greed to blind you to the planet's suffering.&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually there is a proment were-beast faction in the BNS version of WtA. Or at least a fan game based on it by it called the Dawn tribes made up of regional branches of the Fera along with two North american garou tibes who left the nation during the Apocalypse and a pro-kinfolk activist group. They even got J. F. Sambrano on the writing and he has posted his work on his patron (granted it's behind a 5$ paywall last time I checked): <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/c/jfsambrano/posts?vanity=jfsambrano\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.patreon.com/c/jfsambrano...ity=jfsambrano</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":".  Aovid double posting. 03-01-2026, 09:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-01T18:25:40-08:00","id":1558579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558578#post1558578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Again in BNS nearly all the cearns was blown up by the Apocalypse but the nation still stands.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> On the subject of caerns, reclaiming them is going to be a main focus for the BNS version from what little I've read. Either as a reward for the players efforts for securing a area or it's going to be a focus of a episodic campaign where players go around amerca helping isolated septs reclaim they cearns. Which is a step up from what W is offering narrative wise since all the Small victories might actually contribute larger victory.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Well evil guy that might have a point is a oddly prevalent trope in current left presenting media land scape.</div> </div> </div> </div>The funny thing is, Weaver's long term plan is inherently self defeating.<br /> <br /> Weaver wants to solidify the Umbra and keep everything in stasis for all eternity. But what they don't realize is that the gauntlet makes it more difficult for spirits to interact with the material world.<br /> <br /> Guess what, Weaver... YOU'RE A SPIRIT!<br /> <br /> If they manage to seal off the Umbra completely, Weaver has no way to interact with humanity. So they have to leave some sort of access point open to keep their plans in motion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-01T18:48:06-08:00","id":1558580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558579#post1558579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The funny thing is, Weaver's long term plan is inherently self defeating.<br /> <br /> Weaver wants to solidify the Umbra and keep everything in stasis for all eternity. But what they don't realize is that the gauntlet makes it more difficult for spirits to interact with the material world.<br /> <br /> Guess what, Weaver... YOU'RE A SPIRIT!<br /> <br /> If they manage to seal off the Umbra completely, Weaver has no way to interact with humanity. So they have to leave some sort of access point open to keep their plans in motion.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's beside the point. The Weaver doesn't care about interaction with anything; just with studying and understanding the laws and principles of the universe and making sense of the cosmos and its patterns. They're basically breaking down reality to sculpt it like mashed potatoes in a manner not unlike Christopher Walken in <i>Communion</i>, and then declaring &quot;This means something!&quot;<br /> <br /> If the Weaver calcifies and dies, that would definitely be a problem, but they're kind of insane, and would probably assume that they would hypothetically manage to take care of themselves somehow even if they basically turned into a Supernal Hikkikomori hell bent on documenting Pepe Silvia and how he figures into everything before moving onto the next &quot;mystery&quot;, then the next, and the next, etc. No telling if they get anywhere before suffering the same fate as everything they're studying, frozen in time and space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude18","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-02T07:11:38-08:00","id":1558586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558577#post1558577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would also give the other Fera more of a chance to shine, and demonstrate just how badly flawed the Garou were.<br /> <br /> Rokea were specifically tasked with surviving the Apocalypse and helping to repopulate the world after it's passing. This means that Gaia foresaw the Garou would lose the war, and made a contingency for just such an occasion.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Kitsune were promised to not only survive the Apocalypse, but that they would also be granted a purpose once it was all set and done. A post apocalyptic setting would have been a great way to introduce that, instead of having them sit around in Asia waiting for Gaia to give them orders.<br /> <br /> <br /> Then we've got the Makole, who's ability to tap into the memories of the entire planet would have been great way to ensure that people in that setting avoid repeating the mistakes of the past and work towards establishing a better future. &quot;Don't be a raging maniac, and don't allow corporate greed to blind you to the planet's suffering.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>What W5 ended up doing with the Fera is also another one of those hallmarks of W5's problems. One of the currents that runs through the W5 corebook is how a lot of lore was removed and just covered up with a &quot;Who knows what's true?&quot;-attitude. The other Shifters are one of those cases that fall victim to this.<br /> <br /> On pg. 284 it says:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Garou suppose the existence of others similar to themselves \u2014 if not in outlook, then in the ability to assume the mantle of beast and human. Are they allies? Enemies? Reluctant siblings in Gaia? None can say, exactly, and conjecture almost certainly varies day to day.<br /> <br /> [ ... ]<br /> <br /> What Do They Want: The Garou wish they knew, for it might make interacting with these other shapechangers less volatile. Sometimes, other shifters indicate that some long-ago grudge shaped the relationship the Garou have with them today \u2014 which would certainly be in keeping with today\u2019s Garou bearing the responsibility of past times of legend. </div> </div> </div>I always thought this one was particularly funny because it suggests that in the W5 timeline the War of Rage and all that trouble with the Fera still happened but somehow the Garou of the present have completely forgotten about it - except the Fera still managed to remember what happened.<br /> <br /> In the official W5 version, the Garou don't even know Shifters like the Kitsune and Mokole exist!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558578#post1558578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well evil guy that might have a point is a oddly prevalent trope in current left presenting media land scape.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The adventure just assumes he's wrong. But this was another one of those moments where I thought &quot;As long as this guy doesn't simply shrug his shoulders when he encounters Black Spiral Dancers or the like, honestly who cares whether he thinks the Weaver is worse than the Wyrm.&quot; Especially with the Garou Nation gone, who cares how unorthodox his beliefs are. But the adventure clearly states &quot;Alejandro is the Sept Leader. Having participated in the Rite of Balance Bound three times, he\u2019s grown devout in his beliefs that the Weaver is the true enemy. Though he doesn\u2019t realize it, he\u2019s teetering on the precipice of complete corruption.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think the adventure would've worked better if the PCs could've seen his beliefs in action a la &quot;Because of my belief that the Weaver is the true enemy, this Sept is gonna do x.&quot;. And then have the PCs make a judgment about that. Instead of having this very abstract lore-debate be the finale of the adventure... unless the PCs decide to just beat the crap out of him which... is one way to settle a debate, I guess lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-02T09:10:58-08:00","id":1558587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558586#post1558586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always thought this one was particularly funny because it suggests that in the W5 timeline the War of Rage and all that trouble with the Fera still happened but somehow the Garou of the present have completely forgotten about it - except the Fera still managed to remember what happened..</div> </div> </div> </div>It itself is insane<br /> Humans mastered the art of Oral history preservation<br /> Oral tradition has been the primary mode of human communication for tens of thousands of years<br /> Australian Aboriginal oral traditions have preserved accounts of sea-level changes from <b>13,000 to 10,000 BCE</b>. Australian Aboriginal oral histories also appear to reflect volcanic eruptions that occurred between <b>34,000 and 40,000 years ago</b>. Ancient cultures used mnemonic techniques, song, and poetry to transmit history with high precision over generations.<br /> The Garou.. somehow managed to fail in that simpel task<br /> And that is just the Oral history preservation! Lets assume every elder died, everyone, literally everyone who knew the stories, the songs, everything just died... even then fragemnts shoud have remained in the memories of the kids hearg these things as, well kids.<br /> But the Garou Language and &quot;civilization&quot; was not like the speakers of Yuchi; two of the last elderly who spoke that language and knew the stories died 2016 and 2021 making the language funcitonally extinct or the Juma of Brazil; last known member, Aruk\u00e1 Juma, died in 2021... they are around and kicking and there are the Spirits and even Ghosts who know probably whats happened...<br /> Not to mention the Garou is not just a spoken but a written language... the Garou glyphs/runes are still a thing; craved on bone, weapons, stone walls... yet nothing<br /> <br /> Hell, elephants pass down vital knowledge through generations primarily led by older matriarchs who act as repositories of information. This learned wisdom includes mapping migration routes, locating water sources during droughts, and identifying predators.<br /> Younger elephants learn these survival skills through social observation and following the matriarch<br /> Crows pass down knowledge to their offspring and other members of their floc, demonstrating advanced social learning and cultural transmission. They can communicate specific, long-term information about threats\u2014such as dangerous human faces\u2014for up to 17 years, causing younger birds to avoid or mob individuals they have never personally encountered\u200b<br /> <br /> A W5 Garou somehow managed to fail what elephants \u200b\u200b\u200band crows and humans, - now the &quot;primary element&quot; of a Garou - mastered while having a functional, spoen and written language...<br /> <br /> Chirst, even Wolves pass down knowledge across generations, creating unique pack cultures. Older, experienced wolves teach younger members essential skills, including specialized hunting strategies, den site selection, and territory navigation. This social learning ensures that valuable survival techniques, such as adapting to specific weather or terrain, are passed down...<br /> <br /> \u200bBut okay, even Humans forgot history and language... but not things thta happened a decade ago! <br /> And even that required mass murdering whole cilvilizations and trying really hard to erase History and Cultures - we worked HARD to be oblivious of our own past...<br /> The W5 Garou don't have this excuse ...<br /> <br /> The Topic's original queston was: why the Garou Nation so much worse in W5<br /> This<br /> Mostly because of this<br /> Because W5 as a whole is a chaotic insane mess a whole different Game that - I am sure have some very cool elements and concepts (not see those but thats a &quot;me problem&quot; - as a whole is a damn insult anything Werewolf the Apocalypse was (and frenkly, still is) for three damn decade!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-02T11:47:42-08:00","id":1558589,"title":"","content":"Well the oral tradition thing was mostly a handwave so they didnt have to provide a well written history...its why they said their history was purely oral in the first place","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-02T12:31:21-08:00","id":1558590,"title":"","content":"Here's the truly crazy part about the whole &quot;oral history&quot; thing and forgetting their culture and history: The most recent supplement Moonlit Path addressed this. There's a sidebar in the Introduction called &quot;Oral History&quot; and here's what it says:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Much, even most, of Garou history is lost. To speak of an oral tradition is a misnomer. Rather, it comprises multiple traditions separated by geography. Writing down the legends of the Garou is frowned upon as threatening the Veil, and many werewolves see study and research as wasting valuable time when they should be bringing the fight to the Wyrm where many of them fall, taking their knowledge with them. Compounding the problem is that the Garou are not a culture one is born into. Rare is the one who hears the stories of Gaia\u2019s chosen from their childhood. Those joining their ranks are usually young adults, already preoccupied with the concerns of life in this modern world. </div> </div> </div>(You can find the entire sidebar <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1551987-w5-and-garou-oral-tradition\">here</a>. It was part of the preview for Moonlit Path,)<br /> <br /> God, I forgot how this attempt at an explanation makes it even worse. First, the history was at times vague in previous editions because it was oral history, then in the W5 corebook it seemed to blame oral culture for why Garou forgot their history but with this supplement it now has morphed into &quot;Actually Garou don't even really have an oral culture. The real issue is that memorializing Garou culture and history is just too hard, you know. So why bother?&quot;.<br /> <br /> The same way the key-terms like &quot;Age of Apocalypse&quot; and &quot;Gaia's dead/dying&quot; make a post-apocalyptic setting feel like a natural conclusion, I always thought that the natural conclusion to this whole &quot;Who knows?&quot;-business was to wonder why anybody would even bother to call themselves Garou then? If most werewolves barely know anything about the Garou's culture and history, and what little is known is all connected to their failures and how those are tied to this dismal state of the world... why bother calling yourself a Garou? Most of the Spirits (according to W5) don't like Garou, the other Shapeshifters don't like Garou, the Cult of Fenris don't like them, the Black Spiral Dancers don't like them etc., etc. And the Garou apparently don't even care to preserve their own culture and history. It doesn't seem like they even like themselves!<br /> <br /> And to return to the original intent of this thread, that's why W5 is so different to 1st edition. That's why I call it &quot;antipathy&quot;. I really don't get the impression that this edition even likes the idea of Garou. And yet it's so bizarre that despite this, you're supposed to play the most vanilla bogstandard version of a Garou in this edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-02T12:57:00-08:00","id":1558591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558587#post1558587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Snip</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair a home brew did actually try to explain things by having the Garou being forced to preform a &quot;Doomsday rite&quot; that was ment to stop the Wyrm from taking over the Umbra but it caused major spiritual disruption that amoung other things prevents potential garous from undergoing the frist change and it severed the kinfolk from they spiritual link to the garou so they're effectively ordinary humans, meaning as far as the nation knows they're the last generation of garou.<br /> <br /> It's was only after about 3 decades did any new garou undergone they first change and the nation has fractured due sheer attention. So it's less that the Nation forgot they history but the players would have have a hard accessing it due to all the relevant people scattered to the four winds or just dead.<br /> <br /> <br /> But yeah the thing stinks of Pentex propaganda and I'd personally think the whole setting is sort of a matrix like situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-02T13:08:27-08:00","id":1558592,"title":"","content":"So, how long until they just scrap Rage and have them start drinking blood and preying on the living?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-02T13:25:31-08:00","id":1558593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558586#post1558586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I always thought this one was particularly funny because it suggests that in the W5 timeline the War of Rage and all that trouble with the Fera still happened but somehow the Garou of the present have completely forgotten about it - except the Fera still managed to remember what happened.<br /> <br /> In the official W5 version, the Garou don't even know Shifters like the Kitsune and Mokole exist!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Given how they were prone to violent outbursts and had a warrior culture, it's not too surprising. The ones that got hunted to extinction were probably registered as a footnote, or even completely forgotten about, since they were no longer relevant.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Garou:</b> &quot;Am I supposed to know who you are?&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Fera:</b> &quot;You slaughtered our ancestors!&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Garou:</b> &quot;Do you have any idea how little that narrows it down?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-02T13:34:29-08:00","id":1558594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558593#post1558593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Given how they were prone to violent outbursts and had a warrior culture, it's not too surprising. The ones that got hunted to extinction were probably registered as a footnote, or even completely forgotten about, since they were no longer relevant.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Garou:</b> &quot;Am I supposed to know who you are?&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Fera:</b> &quot;You slaughtered our ancestors!&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Garou:</b> &quot;Do you have any idea how little that narrows it down?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Again a BNS fan game actually does have Frea alliance and they lore is party written by J. F. Sambrano.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-02T13:38:19-08:00","id":1558595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558590#post1558590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> God, I forgot how this attempt at an explanation makes it even worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't the Veil a relatively new law among the Garou?<br /> <br /> From what I understand, they adopted a vow of secrecy after they accidentally pissed off the Technocracy, who retaliated by wiping a bunch of them out of consensus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-02T17:01:19-08:00","id":1558604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558595#post1558595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wasn't the Veil a relatively new law among the Garou?<br /> <br /> From what I understand, they adopted a vow of secrecy after they accidentally pissed off the Technocracy, who retaliated by wiping a bunch of them out of consensus?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, when they got together to hammer out the Litany, the Garou made &quot;The Veil Shall Not Be Lifted&quot; as one of its tenets. It's just gotten more important as it's moved from &quot;We're voluntarily not interfering with humanity like we used to&quot; and on into &quot;If we reveal ourselves, we will die.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude18","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-02T22:42:05-08:00","id":1558609,"title":"","content":"To be fair, it was all fun and slaughter untill around 800 BC, the War of Silver and Iron<br /> The Garou went war against the Fae and taught humanity about the restricting power of cold iron.<br /> The Fae (specifically the Sidhe) answered by teaching humanity the power of silver...<br /> From there it was downhill <br /> <br /> Of course in one version of the stories\u200b, but a pretty good version in my humble opinion","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-03T12:03:19-08:00","id":1558622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558609#post1558609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, it was all fun and slaughter untill around 800 BC, the War of Silver and Iron<br /> The Garou went war against the Fae and taught humanity about the restricting power of cold iron.<br /> The Fae (specifically the Sidhe) answered by teaching humanity the power of silver...<br /> From there it was downhill<br /> <br /> Of course in one version of the stories, but a pretty good version in my humble opinion</div> </div> </div> </div>According to Shattered Dreams (&quot;Poison - 5,000 BCE&quot;) and a general date when humans started mining and refining gold and silver, given the appearance of worked items at archeological sites... the fae were like four millennia late to the party. The Changers started using them against each other and the humans noticed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-06T15:42:23-08:00","id":1558689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558478#post1558478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> An ideal. Humans are historically bad at living up to those in the face of practicality. Also, the idealized top of the heap wouldn't get anywhere without the navigators, or still afford boats without the merchant side of the culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>Saying things like this is what allowed Autumn People and the Technocracy to gain a strangle hold over the world.<br /> <br /> Dreams and magic are dying, because they kept telling society that they 'aren't realistic.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-06T17:00:46-08:00","id":1558690,"title":"","content":"In folklore the Fae are quite well known for barter and trade. I\u2019d say they are the merchant side of their culture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-06T17:42:30-08:00","id":1558692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558689#post1558689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Saying things like this is what allowed Autumn People and the Technocracy to gain a strangle hold over the world.<br /> <br /> Dreams and magic are dying, because they kept telling society that they 'aren't realistic.'</div> </div> </div> </div>A topic best left to the Changeling sub-forum; this is the splatter main sub-forum. Changelings in a W:tA game are going to have much more immediately threatening problems, like gorehounds trying to murder them and store what's left in jars or packs of Dancers flinging horrible toxic shit that melts skin everywhere. Or dealt a simultaneously Banal and body horror end by becoming Enfolded due to Chulorviosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-06T18:15:19-08:00","id":1558693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558692#post1558692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A topic best left to the Changeling sub-forum; this is the splatter main sub-forum. Changelings in a W:tA game are going to have much more immediately threatening problems, like gorehounds trying to murder them and store what's left in jars or packs of Dancers flinging horrible toxic shit that melts skin everywhere. Or dealt a simultaneously Banal and body horror end by becoming Enfolded due to Chulorviosis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that much of a threat, when Changelings are capable of performing Arch Mage level feats straight out of character creation.<br /> <br /> Also, which noble House was it that has a history of riding Garou into battle?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-06T19:07:41-08:00","id":1558694,"title":"","content":"No fae noble house has a history of riding Garou into battle. For some reason the CtD authors decided to insert a common story about this into their culture, but no other texts in the WoD games support that it ever happened. One of those things best left out of a WtA specific discussion since somehow it never comes up in the WtA books.... only proving Saur Ops's point a bit there instead of scoring any smart-ass points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-06T23:21:34-08:00","id":1558698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558694#post1558694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No fae noble house has a history of riding Garou into battle. For some reason the CtD authors decided to insert a common story about this into their culture, but no other texts in the WoD games support that it ever happened. One of those things best left out of a WtA specific discussion since somehow it never comes up in the WtA books.... only proving Saur Ops's point a bit there instead of scoring any smart-ass points.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How are they a &quot;smart-ass&quot; for commenting on material found in other splat books? You realize the metaplot tried (and failed) to connect all the splats into a shared universe?<br /> <br /> <br /> I have been informed that mythologically accurate valkyries road across the northern lights on the back of flying wolves.<br /> <br /> As for those riding <b>Garou</b>, I think that might have been <b>Aesin</b>; seeing as they're associated with Norse culture. They also openly state the <b>Fianna</b> are their allies in the relationship section, as were the <b>Fenrir</b> until an ancient mistake drove a wedge between them.<br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> But this is a Werewolf forum, so yes, we should refocus on that.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-07T00:08:45-08:00","id":1558699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558698#post1558698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How are they a &quot;smart-ass&quot; for commenting on material found in other splat books?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But this is a Werewolf forum, so yes, we should refocus on that. </div> </div> </div>Seems like you already know the answer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have been informed that mythologically accurate valkyries road across the northern lights on the back of flying wolves. </div> </div> </div>Well, that's a perfectly vague appeal.<br /> <br /> Anyone that tells you that anything about Norse religion can be strictly stated as accurate (instead of things like possible or plausible) has some serious proving to do to you before you parrot what they say. Our current knowledge of what pre-Christian Norse beliefs were is extremely fragmented and difficult to parse from the influence of later scholars who were the primary sources of records of Norse myths.<br /> <br /> In the extant texts we have, the Valkyries are predominantly presented as riding on horses if anything. The animal they are most associated with (in a plurality at best) were swans. While there are certainly texts that associate them with wolves and ravens but that's difficult to disentangle from their service to Odin; as Odin is very associated with wolves and ravens. While there is quiet probably a text that describes the Valkyries as riding flying wolves, it would be come from a tradition of epic poetry and would need some serious analysis to separate artistic license from transmission of cultural beliefs about them.<br /> <br /> Of course, we have more than texts. We have surviving artifacts such as stones and amulets that depict female warriors that seem to part of the Valkyrie mythological tradition. Everyone of those that has one riding something, it's a horse. <br /> <br /> If you want to go write some fantasy stories and want to spice up your Valkyries without stray from things with basis in Norse mythology? Sure, make them wolf riders (or boar riders, or bear riders, or just give them each different big tough animals that help communicate their individual personalities). What to make a point about how to handle these things in WtA? Yeah, that's not really going to fly.<br /> <br /> I've also recently written up exactly why the C20 prodigals section (and it's 2e precursor) are best ignored in crossover in a different thread if you'd like a larger break down of that. But the basic point is simple: C20 contradicts the other games frequently in that section make it a detriment to attempts to merge the games to include it as it creates more problems that it even tries to solve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude18","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-07T02:03:52-08:00","id":1558700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558699#post1558699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, that's a perfectly vague appeal.<br /> <br /> Anyone that tells you that anything about Norse religion can be strictly stated as accurate (instead of things like possible or plausible) has some serious proving to do to you before you parrot what they say. Our current knowledge of what pre-Christian Norse beliefs were is extremely fragmented and difficult to parse from the influence of later scholars who were the primary sources of records of Norse myths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I'm aware most of the accurate records were erased by crusaders and the like. It's one of the reasons why Galliard Group has such a bad view of the Verbena... the other reason is that they think using seminal fluid and period blood for spell casting is super gross.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558699#post1558699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If you want to go write some fantasy stories and want to spice up your Valkyries without stray from things with basis in Norse mythology? Sure, make them wolf riders (or boar riders, or bear riders, or just give them each different big tough animals that help communicate their individual personalities). What to make a point about how to handle these things in WtA? Yeah, that's not really going to fly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, riding bears sounds like it might be very comfy. Sitting on all that warm fluff while traveling through the cold north.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-07T13:59:18-08:00","id":1558710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558700#post1558700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, I'm aware most of the accurate records were erased by crusaders and the like. It's one of the reasons why Galliard Group has such a bad view of the Verbena... the other reason is that they think using seminal fluid and period blood for spell casting is super gross.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Galliard Group doesn\u2019t like the Verbena because they think they are based on unreliable records of the Norse? Or they don\u2019t like them because they think they destroyed records of the Norse?<br /> <br /> Both are wrong, I just want to know which way they are getting it wrong. The Verbena are not solely or even mostly based on Norse culture, and they didn\u2019t have anything to do with destroying records of it. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-07T14:04:27-08:00","id":1558711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558693#post1558693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not that much of a threat, when Changelings are capable of performing Arch Mage level feats straight out of character creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a lot of provisos that you're skipping over with that. While you're trying to use a bunk, a gorehound has already leapt out of the bushes with a machete. Prep time is nice but a supernatural serial killer is probably going to take steps to prevent you from doing that without even understanding what's going on (they're just trying to provoke jump scares before the end, most likely).<br /> <br /> And if you go through those, there's a good chance a Freakfoot does you in when you have to use the bathroom - perhaps the ultimate dumb, pointless death. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, riding bears sounds like it might be very comfy. Sitting on all that warm fluff while traveling through the cold north.</div> </div> </div> </div>Up until the bear decides it's time for rikosinot, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude18","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-07T14:42:12-08:00","id":1558712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558710#post1558710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Galliard Group doesn\u2019t like the Verbena because they think they are based on unreliable records of the Norse? Or they don\u2019t like them because they think they destroyed records of the Norse?<br /> <br /> Both are wrong, I just want to know which way they are getting it wrong. The Verbena are not solely or even mostly based on Norse culture, and they didn\u2019t have anything to do with destroying records of it.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not just the Norse, I mean paganism in general. So many records of these ancient religions were erased from history, that we don't actually know anything about what these people genuinely believed in. Just bits and pieces we've managed to scrape together, with the rest of it being filled in by fantasy writers and pop culture.<br /> <br /> Consequently, I believe they also had a low opinion of D&amp;D Druids for the same reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-07T15:45:55-08:00","id":1558715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558700#post1558700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, I'm aware most of the accurate records were erased by crusaders and the like. It's one of the reasons why Galliard Group has such a bad view of the Verbena... the other reason is that they think using seminal fluid and period blood for spell casting is super gross.<br /> <br /> Not just the Norse, I mean paganism in general. So many records of these ancient religions were erased from history, that we don't actually know anything about what these people genuinely believed in. Just bits and pieces we've managed to scrape together, with the rest of it being filled in by fantasy writers and pop culture.<br /> <br /> Consequently, I believe they also had a low opinion of D&amp;D Druids for the same reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope that &quot;Galliard Group&quot; you mentioned was a bit more detailed with their opinions because all of that sounds like quite the glib overgeneralization...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.p