uote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558716#post1558716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unfortunately not. Whenever the Verbena are brought up on their podcasts, they almost always jump at the chance to joke about how they use semen and <b>minstrel blood</b> to cast their spells. One episode even had them suggest the Verbena just drops their pants and begin shitting on the floor mid combat.<br /> <br /> Like I said, they aren't particularly fond of them.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I guess that's one way to cut down on racist performance art...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-07T17:39:36-08:00","id":1558719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558716#post1558716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unfortunately not. Whenever the Verbena are brought up on their podcasts, they almost always jump at the chance to joke about how they use semen and minstrel blood to cast their spells. One episode even had them suggest the Verbena just drops their pants and begin shitting on the floor mid combat.<br /> <br /> Like I said, they aren't particularly fond of them.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Okay... I assume you're watching their content since you brought them up - but in your portrayal of them, they're looking worse with each description you offer...? I dread to wonder what these people think about other groups in the WOD if that's how they treat the Verbena. <br /> <br /> And then, it doesn't really add to the conversation to bring up these clowns. I get it, they like to make crude jokes and they're making sweeping, uninformed statements about history... at least, that's my impression of them thus far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude18","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-07T19:21:07-08:00","id":1558721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558716#post1558716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unfortunately not. Whenever the Verbena are brought up on their podcasts, they almost always jump at the chance to joke about how they use semen and minstrel blood to cast their spells. One episode even had them suggest the Verbena just drops their pants and begin shitting on the floor mid combat.<br /> <br /> Like I said, they aren't particularly fond of them.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Which is funny, as they've said multiple times the Fianna are one of their favorite tribes, and they're angry that they've been stripped off their Irish heritage in 5th edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-07T19:29:36-08:00","id":1558722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558719#post1558719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay... I assume you're watching their content since you brought them up - but in your portrayal of them, they're looking worse with each description you offer...? I dread to wonder what these people think about other groups in the WOD if that's how they treat the Verbena.<br /> <br /> And then, it doesn't really add to the conversation to bring up these clowns. I get it, they like to make crude jokes and they're making sweeping, uninformed statements about history... at least, that's my impression of them thus far.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I can clarify a bit more. DarkKing isn't wrong that they think the portrayal of modern paganism is mostly pop culture fantasy, but they also emphasized that the Verbena book was largely bare bones with not much meat to go on.<br /> <br /> Some of their takes on the various Tribes / Clans / Kiths / Traditions are not in a positive light, that's true. But they do have others which they greatly approve.<br /> <br /> Galliard Group may be 'crude and rude' when it comes to their deep dive videos, but they are also passionate, long time players of the franchise who care about the quality of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-07T20:09:09-08:00","id":1558723,"title":"","content":"As someone that could reasonably be called a crude toeing-the-line-on-rude passionate longtime player of the franchise, I still feel like either the Galliard Group is not a great source for people seeking to have in-depth conversations on that same sort of deep dive level, or there's a disconnect between what they're saying and how that information seems to show up here.<br /> <br /> In any case, it feels like there could be a bit more &quot;here's what the books say,&quot; over, &quot;here's what some podcasters talking about the books say.&quot; Or at least citing podcasts with a bit more access like Josh Heath on his podcast (as someone that's worked on the franchise professionally on top of doing fan content of many stripes).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-08T05:57:30-07:00","id":1558729,"title":"","content":"Yes, Josh Heath is relevant to be brought up. Not only for his fan-content (his podcast) but because he was a playtester for the released W5 version. And what he talked about after the release was that the version that he playtested had even more punishing mechanics than the released version. This also lines up with what I remember Outstar talking about because she was an ST in one of those playtest-sessions as well, and she talked about how she was surprised by how nobody ended up using the Crinos Form. Presumably due to the punishing mechanics, the players simply looked at the Crinos Form and thought &quot;It's not worth it.&quot;.<br /> <br /> This goes to show that the negativity/pessimism isn't just there in the description of the Garou in W5 but the intent also seemed to be there to show that off via the mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude18","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-08T16:38:32-07:00","id":1558737,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558729#post1558729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, Josh Heath is relevant to be brought up. Not only for his fan-content (his podcast) but because he was a playtester for the released W5 version. And what he talked about after the release was that the version that he playtested had even more punishing mechanics than the released version. This also lines up with what I remember Outstar talking about because she was an ST in one of those playtest-sessions as well, and she talked about how she was surprised by how nobody ended up using the Crinos Form. Presumably due to the punishing mechanics, the players simply looked at the Crinos Form and thought &quot;It's not worth it.&quot;.<br /> <br /> This goes to show that the negativity/pessimism isn't just there in the description of the Garou in W5 but the intent also seemed to be there to show that off via the mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well how does that compare to this variant of the Rage manics from the mind eye therater version of WtA<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Rage mechanic from Mind's Eye Theater Werewolf we in the team have grown fond of called Seethe. Seethe represents that smoldering anger deep within every Garou, waiting to burst out, chase, and kill things. The mechanic is straightforward:</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">If something happens to upset, aggravate, annoy, or otherwise perturb your Garou, they gain a point of Seethe, represented as a temporary point of Rage that can go past your permanent Rage score if you let it.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">If your character does not become further aggravated, the Seethe point goes away on its own; you can lose one Seethe per hour in this way. The Garou may spend that Seethe as ordinary Rage to burn it off, as well.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">If your Seethe exceeds your permanent Rage score by 3 dots, you instantly frenzy.</div> <br /> </div> </div> </div>Edit: And another from a W5 hombrew that basically a reskinned harmony bar:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, I did a big overhaul of the morality system too, replaced the two trackers with a single one, hope, which at one end leaves the garou complacent and unable to imagine a better world, while the other end describes iconoclastic and zealous Garou who can't imagine leaving the world as it is </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 03-08-2026, 07:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-08T18:27:30-07:00","id":1558739,"title":"","content":"I don't recall Josh describing the play-test version in enough detail to compare to the final rules fairly; let alone try to compare it to other mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-09T03:13:40-07:00","id":1558743,"title":"","content":"It's from <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DrH7EZXzWmw\" target=\"_blank\">this video</a>. It's around the 2:40 mark where Josh says: &quot;I am going to mention play testing just to say this we play tested a couple of versions of these right. Those were worse. This is better but it's still bad. I don't quite know why they didn't just use the exact same system as hunger dice in Vampire.&quot; I think there were other sections as well. But it's a nearly four hour video. That's just the one I found with some quick searching of the transcript. But that's basically what I'm referring to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude18","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-21T09:05:32-07:00","id":1561993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558429#post1558429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a heads up though, the Galliard Group are passionate fans, not corporate shills. They give their honest, unfiltered takes and opinions about the game, so there is the risk that they might say something you or others find offensive.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the textbook spiel of Alt-Right assholes who want to vomit their prejudice with all the vitriol of their blackened hearts without having to justify anything they say.<br /> <br /> And everything said about them later in this thread just confirms this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558434#post1558434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not quite as extreme as the change between the old Hunter and the new one, but it's still much more significant than the change Vampire got, and a lot of people aren't terribly thrilled about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I beg to disagree.<br /> <br /> H5 is a direct continuation of Hunters Hunted, and all the other hunter-oriented supplements that came after.<br /> <br /> What it did to the legacy of HtR is horrible, but the setting and lore itself is mostly Legacy WoD. The themes also way more compatible.<br /> <br /> And W5 is far from just a deviation from older editions: it is an objectively bad execution at what it tried.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558444#post1558444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, most of the time, every W5-Garou-PC is automatically engaged in this kind of doomspiral. And that isn't just a harsh mechanic compared to previous WtA-editions, it's harsh compared to the other two WOD5E-games.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's harsh compared to Chaosium's Call of Cthulhu Sanity system, and that game was designed to all but guarantee a PC going insane every other session.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558447#post1558447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any claims that they were being used by white supremacists to spread hate speech are complete bullshit. Nazi's have other things to do, than spend hours of their weekly schedule role playing with a bunch of nerdy goths and furries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence such claims have never been made.<br /> <br /> The problem was that some nerdy goths and furries are also Nazis and and used them to go to events, make overtly Nazi characters, annoy everyone else and hide behind roleplay. That's not an argument, is a documented fact.<br /> <br /> And the Get slaying the Swords of Heimdall was exactly the original answer to this, the SoH were originally to stay as a setting element, the Nazis were precisely portraying them. The devs made their extermination a thing precisely to give STs in events an excuse to veto Nazi PCs and justify killing Nazis on sight in the game.<br /> <br /> Paradox went further because Paradox is a coward Corp that violently avoids risks.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558472#post1558472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, selecting the best warriors ... Ragnarok.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of cultures had the concept of great warriors being rewarded in the afterlife. No big deal.<br /> <br /> Observe in particular that Valhalla is specified as a rare fate in the afterlife, even because it's not for every good warrior, it's specifically for those who fall in battle. This is far less people than you imagine, as in most ancient battles very few people would be really killed in the battle itself.<br /> <br /> Many survived even among the defeated, and most deaths were from later complications like gangrene, which doesn't qualify.<br /> <br /> Standard fate in what we know of those myths is the Hall of Hella.<br /> <br /> Ragnarok specifically we don't even know if it's original to the religion or a Christian addendum.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558699#post1558699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've also recently written up exactly why the C20 prodigals section (and it's 2e precursor) are best ignored in crossover in a different thread if you'd like a larger break down of that. But the basic point is simple: C20 contradicts the other games frequently in that section make it a detriment to attempts to merge the games to include it as it creates more problems that it even tries to solve.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't try to solve any problem, which is what I actually like about it.<br /> <br /> Changeling stories about the Prodigals aren't to be taken seriously. The Fae themselves don't track those legends or pay much attention. The other splats are called Prodigals because they <i>assume</i> all magic comes from the Dreaming and that's about it.<br /> <br /> Even in a crossover I'd suggest to have them believing those and other legends (they have many and they contradict). And even in a game of Changeling I'd suggest to not take any of them seriously.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558700#post1558700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I'm aware most of the accurate records were erased by crusaders and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no accurate records. Their religion was strictly passed through oral tradition with very few names written in ogham.<br /> <br /> All the written stories are by later Christian authors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1558437#post1558437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This goes back to a central idea in the game, that you can't beat the Wyrm by being a raging ball of violence and rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>By the way, WtA always had this theme.<br /> <br /> The game has always been very clear that the pure violence approach is the reason the Garou are in their current situation. The hope comes a lot from it being possible to change the Garou Nation in this regard.<br /> <br /> Violence still solves a lot of things, but must be better directed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-21T13:20:59-07:00","id":1562004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1561993#post1561993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's the textbook spiel of Alt-Right assholes who want to vomit their prejudice with all the vitriol of their blackened hearts without having to justify anything they say.<br /> <br /> And everything said about them later in this thread just confirms this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except for the fact the Galliad group includes<br /> <br /> <b>A)</b> People with autism<br /> <br /> <b>B)</b> Openly gay<br /> <br /> <b>C)</b> Jewish<br /> <br /> <b>D)</b> Transgender people<br /> <br /> <b>E)</b> Feminists<br /> <br /> The Black Furies are actually one of their favorite tribes, and they were not pleased to see that W5 turned them from the tribe of female empowerment, into generic protectors of the downtrodden.<br /> <br /> -------------------<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1561993#post1561993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A lot of cultures had the concept of great warriors being rewarded in the afterlife. No big deal.<br /> <br /> Observe in particular that Valhalla is specified as a rare fate in the afterlife, even because it's not for every good warrior, it's specifically for those who fall in battle. This is far less people than you imagine, as in most ancient battles very few people would be really killed in the battle itself.<br /> <br /> Many survived even among the defeated, and most deaths were from later complications like gangrene, which doesn't qualify.<br /> <br /> Standard fate in what we know of those myths is the Hall of Hella.<br /> <br /> Ragnarok specifically we don't even know if it's original to the religion or a Christian addendum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you had to die in battle with a weapon in your hand, I believe.<br /> <br /> Which is probably not something the Get would have struggled with, given their reputation.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-21T13:29:02-07:00","id":1562006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1562004#post1562004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except for the fact the Galliad group includes<br /> <br /> <b>A)</b> People with autism<br /> <br /> <b>B)</b> Openly gay<br /> <br /> <b>C)</b> Jewish<br /> <br /> <b>D)</b> Transgender people<br /> <br /> <b>E)</b> Feminists<br /> <br /> The Black Furies are actually one of their favorite tribes, and they were not pleased to see that W5 turned them from the tribe of female empowerment, into generic protectors of the downtrodden.<br /> <br /> -------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah, you had to die in battle with a weapon in your hand, I believe.<br /> <br /> Which is probably not something the Get would have struggled with, given their reputation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being leftwing doesn't stop someone from behaving horribly, I guess. Either way I've seen no indication of relevant opinions, only people who want to justify anything shit they vomit.<br /> <br /> Seen a lot of those among Autistics, LGBTQIAP+ people, Jews and Feminists, they're not magically exempt.<br /> <br /> What the Get could manage or not has nothing to do with the actual human culture of ancient and medieval Scandinavia, and they're not in the business of waiting for Valkyries anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-21T13:33:12-07:00","id":1562007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1562006#post1562006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Being leftwing doesn't stop someone from behaving horribly, I guess. Either way I've seen no indication of relevant opinions, only people who want to justify anything shit they vomit.<br /> <br /> Seen a lot of those among Autistics, LGBTQIAP+ people, Jews and Feminists, they're not magically exempt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, nice to see someone finally had the courage to up and admit it. I was afraid the leftist had become a mindless cult by now.<br /> <br /> Unless you aren't a leftist. In which case, I apologize for assuming.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1562006#post1562006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What the Get could manage or not has nothing to do with the actual human culture of ancient and medieval Scandinavia, and they're not in the business of waiting for Valkyries anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the Get aren't human; and as I believe has already been pointed out on these forums &quot;Garou culture is not human culture&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 07-21-2026, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-21T15:26:02-07:00","id":1562013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1562007#post1562007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow, nice to see someone finally had the courage to up and admit it. I was afraid the leftist had become a mindless cult by now</div> </div> </div> </div>I am a leftist and have the general view I try not to assume that everyone is following dogma without questioning. <br /> <br /> I think it's a bad attitude to have.<br /> <br /> But social media encourages group dismissal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-21T15:40:40-07:00","id":1562014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1562013#post1562013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But social media encourages group dismissal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, but probably best left to a different thread.<br /> <br /> Or even PM discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-21T16:12:58-07:00","id":1562015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas;m1561993</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I beg to disagree.<br /> <br /> H5 is a direct continuation of Hunters Hunted, and all the other hunter-oriented supplements that came after.<br /> <br /> What it did to the legacy of HtR is horrible, but the setting and lore itself is mostly Legacy WoD. The themes also way more compatible.<br /> <br /> And W5 is far from just a deviation from older editions: it is an objectively bad execution at what it tried.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll note that Hunters Hunted and Hunters Hunted II were both Vampire: the Masquerade books, not Hunter: the Reckoning books. So yes, H5 is a direct continuation of the VtM Hunters Hunted books, not a direction continuation of Hunter: the Reckoning. There was some overlap in that in both games you're fighting supernatural beings (primarily vampires with Hunters Hunted) but there were always some clear fundamental differences between H:tR and HH and they were never the same game, even back when HtR released or when Hunters Hunted II released.<br /> <br /> Again, the fundamental issue is that H5 is not an update or continuation of HtR. It's a different game and functionally replaces Hunter: the Reckoning with Hunters Hunted. It's a bit like if V5 had replaced all of Kindred with Wan Kuei. Some people would think that was the bees knees, but some people would say that was problematic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-31T14:27:57-07:00","id":1562375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1562015#post1562015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So yes, H5 is a direct continuation of the VtM Hunters Hunted books, not a direction continuation of Hunter: the Reckoning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is, to the letter, what I said.<br /> <br /> And I still disagree that this makes H5 a greater departure from the original game than W5.<br /> <br /> H5 doesn't have the actual original splat, this is incredibly offensive and stupid, but it has more or less the same setting, or at least the same meta-setting, similar themes, similar role...<br /> <br /> But W5 doesn't have the actual original splat and doesn't have any of those other things. It's literally and entirely different game casually using the same words. In <i>my</i> understanding this is objectively worse, and that's what I meant.<br /> <br /> In no way I think any of the two should have happened, and if you search my posts of the time of H5 release you'll see how pissed I was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-31T23:02:04-07:00","id":1562409,"title":"","content":"The irony is they could have included Imbued rules for Hunter: The Reckoning. Make them a faction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-31T23:18:52-07:00","id":1562416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/