iner b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1562417#post1562417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Believe me, I'm a Chicago fan so I know what it's like to have the developers want to never reference your stuff again.</div> </div> </div> </div> To be fair from what little seen of 6E aside from The obvious Controversial maniacal changes (though personally I think free clan disciplines could translate nicely to free aspice and/or tribal gifts and Forsaken style humanity bar could replace the current harano/Hauglosk bars) it seems to be back to basics on the lore front for V6 at least since the preview mention massive roll back on V5 lore. <br /> <br /> Though it seems when parwolf try to please everyone they are going please no one. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-01T09:40:24-07:00","id":1562430,"title":"","content":"Having actual rules for Harano isn't a bad idea, despite W5 execution being horrible, and I could get behind Hauglosk in a balancing scale mechanic.<br /> <br /> I'd say though that Hauglosk isn't a state that makes you into a White Supremacist pseudo viking, but instead that it is subtle but common state among the Elders of the Garou Nation, explaining their extreme attachment to unadaptive traditions and refusal to change a lot of prejudice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-01T13:03:32-07:00","id":1562438,"title":"","content":"The only lack of rules with Harano is how far you have to be pushed to get it. After you do have it, 2e and Revised have pretty detailed rules for what your struggle with it will be mechanically. Having it not be a character sheet collection mechanic is probably better than where it stands in W5.<br /> <br /> (Also, the Silver Fang Lodge of the Moon has a rank one Gift that can hold it at bay for a limited amount of time - Full Moon Cleansing)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-01T14:35:12-07:00","id":1562444,"title":"","content":"I don't remember that rule. How's it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-01T17:44:42-07:00","id":1562451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1562430#post1562430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having actual rules for Harano isn't a bad idea, despite W5 execution being horrible, and I could get behind Hauglosk in a balancing scale mechanic.<br /> <br /> I'd say though that Hauglosk isn't a state that makes you into a White Supremacist pseudo viking, but instead that it is subtle but common state among the Elders of the Garou Nation, explaining their extreme attachment to unadaptive traditions and refusal to change a lot of prejudice.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know V6 clan exclusive frenzy could technically be adapted into tribe specific Hauglosk, Like what was initially planed for W5. Like J. F. Sambrano even shared a example on his Patron where the Glass wakers under it's effect basically go full tech bro (&quot;I dont care if my ai data-center is draining the lake, it's so close to figuring how to seal away the wyrm for ever&quot;).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 08-02-2026, 03:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T02:51:42-07:00","id":1562467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1562444#post1562444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't remember that rule. How's it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Willpower (diff 7) every scene where you make rolls, to see if your dice pool is halved or not, or spend a point instead.<br /> <br /> If you manage to succeed at a difficult and significant task, Willpower (diff 10) to see if you can push back against Harano. Success means you stop having to make the above roll, and gain a permanent Willpower point, but every new moon you have to make a diff 5 roll to see if you relapse. You don't gain permanent Willpower from overcoming any future relapses.<br /> <br /> (Revised Player's Guide to Garou, p 226)<br /> <br /> Full Moon Cleansing allows you to spend Rage to make a Rage roll instead, or potentially as a second chance to avoid slipping for the scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T07:00:39-07:00","id":1562480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1562467#post1562467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Willpower (diff 7) every scene where you make rolls, to see if your dice pool is halved or not, or spend a point instead.<br /> <br /> If you manage to succeed at a difficult and significant task, Willpower (diff 10) to see if you can push back against Harano. Success means you stop having to make the above roll, and gain a permanent Willpower point, but every new moon you have to make a diff 5 roll to see if you relapse. You don't gain permanent Willpower from overcoming any future relapses.<br /> <br /> (Revised Player's Guide to Garou, p 226)<br /> <br /> Full Moon Cleansing allows you to spend Rage to make a Rage roll instead, or potentially as a second chance to avoid slipping for the scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I meant a rule for how you get there. I agree that Harano should be a playable and possible to overcome state, by the way, but we had any rule to tell you're in Harano aside &quot;the ST said so&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T07:13:23-07:00","id":1562482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1562480#post1562480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I meant a rule for how you get there. I agree that Harano should be a playable and possible to overcome state, by the way, but we had any rule to tell you're in Harano aside &quot;the ST said so&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I said as much. The only hard rule for &quot;this definitely causes Harano&quot; is one of the results on the aging chart, just one off from &quot;Dead&quot;. Which just goes to show you how much of a part of the game Harano is i.e. not particularly front and center, kind of an after thought because there weren't really any rules for it until the 2nd edition player's guide came out in 1998, about six years into the game's life.<br /> <br /> (The 1e Player's Guide had an Older Brother Gift that could cause it, but it only lasts for one scene and is seemingly meant to be way more vicious than actual Harano - you can't do anything without making a diff 6 Willpower roll, there)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-02T07:37:17-07:00","id":1562486,"title":"","content":"I'd say that if they do chose to make it post-Apocalypse, it would be interesting to have Harano.<br /> <br /> But I'd play it differently from W5, very different. The Apocalypse as a victory, but not a fix, the world is still broken and in danger, and any forces of destruction still can get it done even if without The Wyrm.<br /> <br /> This version would have the Garou faced with a context where they're still needed, but their role isn't so proudly central. Still highly militaristic, but without a clear war to fight. Overall a post war crisis for the Nation, where their prowess and knowhow is required in a smaller scale than they'd want.<br /> <br /> Not saying this is what the setting should be, but is an option if they don't push the Apocalypse further.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T12:37:34-07:00","id":1562570,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't mind Harano rules.<br /> <br /> But so much of the streamlining seems allergic to the rules existing as a whole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T13:17:28-07:00","id":1562574,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1562486#post1562486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not saying this is what the setting should be, but is an option if they don't push the Apocalypse further.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honstly from what I've seen of V6 it's likely that white wolf will likely try to keep the w5 setting instead of rebooting it, while also rolling back many setting changes to a pre 5e state alongside tacking on something stupid like a mandate against real world politics and focus wrym fighting. .<br /> <br /> Resulting in muddied confused mess that pleases no one. Assuming iWtA gets a 6E in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T14:34:51-07:00","id":1562580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1562570#post1562570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't mind Harano rules.<br /> <br /> But so much of the streamlining seems allergic to the rules existing as a whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, making Harano common is very much a decision to play a drastically different game. It's just not central to the assumed experience like, say, battle scars, keeping up a caern, or having a pack with a spiritual patron. It's not even on the level of maybe fighting the Weaver's minions instead of some Wyrm critter, because the Weaver's side has at the very least been an antagonist since the 1e core book (D.N.A. is a day-one enemy), and received presentations that push them further into the limelight of being the villain of the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T17:26:34-07:00","id":1562599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1562574#post1562574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honstly from what I've seen of V6 it's likely that white wolf will likely try to keep the w5 setting instead of rebooting it, while also rolling back many setting changes to a pre 5e state alongside tacking on something stupid like a mandate against real world politics and focus wrym fighting. .<br /> <br /> Resulting in muddied confused mess that pleases no one. Assuming iWtA gets a 6E in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this follows from anything I saw from the Playtest, and keeping W5 but rolling back W5 doesn't even make sense. Not as in, doesn't make sense for them to do it and more as in, this phrase doesn't make sense.<br /> <br /> V6 is not a thing and probably won't be for the next year, year and a half at least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1562580#post1562580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the other hand, making Harano common is very much a decision to play a drastically different game.</div> </div> </div> </div>But having rules doesn't necessarily makes it common, just clearly defined. The rules for Abominations make them all but impossible to make, and they're very clear, to the last roll.<br /> <br /> If we have something like this new Humanity Scale, falling to Harano would still be hard and rare, and at the same time we could have an in setting explanation for the political positions of Elders by assuming most eventually fall to Hauglosk without noticing or noticing it's even a risk, as they avoid Harano too strongly.<br /> <br /> No, I'm not sure if I want this. Just throwing ideas as they will eventually do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T18:39:59-07:00","id":1562603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1562599#post1562599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think this follows from anything I saw from the Playtest, and keeping W5 but rolling back W5 doesn't even make sense. Not as in, doesn't make sense for them to do it and more as in, this phrase doesn't make sense.<br /> <br /> V6 is not a thing and probably won't be for the next year, year and a half at least.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I meant that white wolf would try and bring things back to a more legacy style setting even if the events required for that to happen comes off as contrived and goes against the foundation W5 was built on in the first place.<br /> <br /> Like best case scenario is that all the tribe name changes back to pre W5 names and the Cult of fenrir just kinda fizzed out which result in the tribe crawling back to that some how spontaneously reformed. I don't want to know what the worse case is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T19:01:58-07:00","id":1562605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1562603#post1562603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I meant that white wolf would try and bring things back to a more legacy style setting even if the events required for that to happen comes off as contrived and goes against the foundation W5 was built on in the first place.<br /> <br /> Like best case scenario is that all the tribe name changes back to pre W5 names and the Cult of fenrir just kinda fizzed out which result in the tribe crawling back to that some how spontaneously reformed. I don't want to know what the worse case is.</div> </div> </div> </div>With W5 that's fundamentally impossible. If things are Legacy style, they're fundamentally not W5 anymore. New lore can be more Legacy style, but backpedaling established lore is basically ditching W5.<br /> <br /> This has nothing to do with V5 because it only requires very soft retcons here and there and the plot advancing forward, because it is already possible.<br /> <br /> In V6, if it stays in course, the Beckoning will slow down until stopping, and the SI lose momentum until their bakers step down and the big operation dies out. Neither denies those things existed.<br /> <br /> How do you rewind W5 without denying W5 existed? How much can it really result in Legacy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T20:19:02-07:00","id":1562608,"title":"","content":"W:tA has had retcons before, which typically do not end up commented upon. Thrall of the Wyrm? A retcon treated as always having been there. Radical differences in how Renown works? A retcon treated as always having been there. Not needing mirrors to step sideways? You get the idea. While going &quot;Poof!&quot; on W5 would undoubtedly be the largest retcon of this sort, it's clearly a potential Mirror Zone diversion that can distract from other retcons, like changing what breed gets called what or how Garou on Garou sex works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1562599#post1562599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But having rules doesn't necessarily makes it common, just clearly defined. The rules for Abominations make them all but impossible to make, and they're very clear, to the last roll.<br /> <br /> If we have something like this new Humanity Scale, falling to Harano would still be hard and rare, and at the same time we could have an in setting explanation for the political positions of Elders by assuming most eventually fall to Hauglosk without noticing or noticing it's even a risk, as they avoid Harano too strongly.<br /> <br /> No, I'm not sure if I want this. Just throwing ideas as they will eventually do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose it depends on how many people in charge of development are hellbent for Harano.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T02:28:18-07:00","id":1562620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1562605#post1562605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How do you rewind W5 without denying W5 existed?</div> </div> </div> </div>From what little I've seen of V6. Poorly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1562608#post1562608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">W:tA has had retcons before, which typically do not end up commented upon. Thrall of the Wyrm? A retcon treated as always having been there. Radical differences in how Renown works? A retcon treated as always having been there. Not needing mirrors to step sideways? You get the idea. While going &quot;Poof!&quot; on W5 would undoubtedly be the largest retcon of this sort, it's clearly a potential Mirror Zone diversion that can distract from other retcons, like changing what breed gets called what or how Garou on Garou sex works.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly one Way I could think of retconning in say the crinos-born is to say that recently after<b> [Insert Metaplot Event Here]</b> results of inter garou parings occasionally has they baby come out in warform which tends to end badly for everyone present for the birth. For the first few years the garou as a whole mostly sees it seen as a blessing since the phonima provides a way to realibly create more warriors of gaia (if you discount the collateral) until those those Born garou have children of they own which come... out wrong and they children's come out more wrong, akin to a bad photo copy. Which is why Lantry cation against inter garou mating. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T06:33:59-07:00","id":1562634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1562620#post1562620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what little I've seen of V6. Poorly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aside that being you shitting on it gratuitously because there's nothing to back up the idea, it's not what I asked.<br /> <br /> Making W6 more similar to Legacy is one thing, but the lore for it will still fundamentally not be Legacy, not be compatible with Legacy, not any lick of a relationship with Legacy. V6 can go to Legacy status quo. W6 can imitate at best. Not the same thing and as such an even more absurd conclusion to draw from the Playtest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T07:39:55-07:00","id":1562641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1558364-query-from-a-casual-why-is-the-garou-nation-so-much-worse-off?p=1562634#post1562634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aside that being you shitting on it gratuitously because there's nothing to back up the idea, it's not what I asked.<br /> <br /> Making W6 more similar to Legacy is one thing, but the lore for it will still fundamentally not be Legacy, not be compatible with Legacy, not any lick of a relationship with Legacy. V6 can go to Legacy status quo. W6 can imitate at best. Not the same thing and as such an even more absurd conclusion to draw from the Playtest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if we rename Younger Brother something different and ditch Hart Wardens in favor of one of the many names that the quasi-tribes under the Fianna historically went by in Revised (while acknowledging that they did, in fact, go by Fianna for a long while), we're retconning W5 out and moving forward from Revised instead.<br /> <br /> Pegasus and Cockroach never left, the Bone Gnawers were never mostly Dogsferatu, and Albrecht is dead, but well-remembered for having taken Zhyzhak with him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core